    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Project Kickoff: Architectural Canon and Groundwork"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1794063483751036400",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "*Time: October 27, 2026, 16:40 (~45 minutes)*"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751037700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Following an in-depth design interview in `/grill-me` mode and full alignment with the ArtCraft (`storytold`) ecosystem standards, the **StatCraft** project is officially launched — an open-source, high-performance statistical suite written in 100% pure Rust."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751039100",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "The master development regulation `AGENTS.md` is codified:\n* Strict compilation limit of `jobs = 1` protecting workstation resources;\n* **Never Crash** principle: complete prohibition of `unwrap()`, `expect()`, `panic!()`, and `unsafe`;\n* Commands rather than handlers architecture (`CommandBus`, AI-agent schemas);\n* Strict L0–L6 layering verified via `cargo xtask layers`;\n* Zero string hardcoding in the UI (`locales/*.ftl`, instant runtime RU/EN switching);\n* 100% mandatory test coverage per function with precision statistical oracles."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751041000",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "---"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751042200",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Phase 1: Workspace Scaffolding, L0/L1/L5 Core, and egui_dock UI"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1794063483751043000",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "*Time: October 27, 2026, 17:05 (~25 minutes)*"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751043800",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Successfully implemented and verified the initial architectural milestone:\n1. **L0 Codecs (`statcraft_io`):** Streaming CSV/TSV parser with automatic delimiter detection (comma/semicolon/tab) and type inference (Numeric / Text / Date) with zero panics.\n2. **L1 Data Engine (`statcraft_core`):** `DataSet` table structure and `VariableDictionary` (scales `Scale`, `Ordinal`, `Nominal`, `ValueLabels` maps, `MissingValues`). Transactional `DeltaBuffer` with cell-level Undo/Redo.\n3. **Zero-Hardcode Localization (`statcraft_i18n`):** Thread-safe Fluent-based catalog engine (`en.ftl` and `ru.ftl`) supporting runtime language switching. `i18n_lint_test` enforces 0% hardcoded literals in UI code.\n4. **L5 Command Bus (`statcraft_syntax`):** Strongly-typed `EngineCommand` bus with JSON schemas for AI agents (`data.import_csv`, `var.set_label`, `var.set_measure`, `data.cell_edit`) and Undo/Redo history.\n5. **L6 Presentation Layer (`statcraft_app`):** Docking workspace on `egui_dock` featuring **Data View** (virtualized grid for 1M+ rows, value labels toggle), **Variable View** (metadata property grid), and **Output Viewer** (outline tree).\n6. **Branding & Vector Icon:** `assets/icon.svg` cleaned of Illustrator export artifacts and rendered natively via the `paint_app_icon` vector widget.\n7. **Testing:** 38 out of 38 unit and integration tests passed cleanly (`cargo test --workspace -j 1`). `cargo clippy` and `cargo fmt` passed with zero warnings."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751045700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "---"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751047000",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Phase 1.1: Comprehensive End-to-End Icon Integration"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1794063483751047500",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "*Time: October 27, 2026, 17:30 (~20 minutes)*"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751048100",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Completed end-to-end integration of the official vector brand icon `assets/icon.svg`:\n1. **Geometry & Centering:** Removed Adobe Illustrator markup bloat, centered the square glyph viewBox (`26 116 560 560`) with zero letterhead margins.\n2. **Multi-resolution Asset Generator (`xtask icon`):** Implemented an automated pipeline based on `resvg` and `ico` generating multi-res PNGs (16, 32, 48, 64, 128, 256 px) and `assets/icon.ico`.\n3. **PE `.exe` Resource Embedding:** Configured `winres` in `build.rs` to embed `icon.ico` directly into the `.rsrc` section of `statcraft_app.exe`. Windows Explorer and the Taskbar now render the official icon.\n4. **Window & Taskbar Integration:** Supplied the rasterized icon via `eframe::icon_data::from_png_bytes` into `ViewportBuilder::with_icon` for native titlebar and Taskbar presence.\n5. **In-App Menu Bar Texture:** Replaced distorted line approximations with a pixel-perfect, crisp texture loaded into egui's context (`egui::TextureHandle`) displayed next to the StatCraft brand name.\n6. **Verification:** All 37 tests green, Clippy and Fmt passed cleanly, and resource extraction verified via `System.Drawing.Icon.ExtractAssociatedIcon`."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751050100",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "---"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751050900",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Phase 1.2: Menu Layout Optimization and Dynamic Localization Fix"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1794063483751051500",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "*Time: October 27, 2026, 17:48 (~15 minutes)*"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751052300",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Refined top layout ergonomics and solved stale string caching in the localization system:\n1. **Menu Bar De-duplication:** Removed duplicate icon and app title from `egui::menu::bar`. The menu items (`File`, `Edit`, `View`, `Data`, `Analyze`) now anchor directly to the top-left client area right below the native Windows titlebar, adhering to desktop UX canon (SPSS, Photoshop).\n2. **Elimination of Stale Localized Strings:** Resolved the apparent \"hardcoded strings\" issue caused by early string materialization in application state (`String` inside `OutputEntry` and `status_message`). When switching languages, old messages lingered in the prior language. Refactored state into semantic types `StatusMessage` and `OutputPayload`, resolving translations dynamically against the active Fluent catalog on each frame.\n3. **Refined Russian Catalog:** Cleaned up English parenthetical suffixes in `locales/ru.ftl` (`Представление данных`, `Представление переменных`, `Просмотр вывода`).\n4. **Verification:** All 38 workspace tests passing with `-j 1`, Clippy and Fmt clean. Release binary built."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751053800",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "---"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751055100",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Phase 1.3: Table Grid Alignment Fix and Pinned Column Headers"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1794063483751055600",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "*Time: October 27, 2026, 18:00 (~15 minutes)*"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751056200",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Resolved table grid column-header misalignment and scrolling defects in both Data View and Variable View:\n1. **Root Cause Analysis:** Using `ui.allocate_ui_with_layout` caused cells to shrink-wrap to the bounding box of their text contents (a cell displaying `\"1\"` took 10 px, a large float took 50 px, headers took 80 px, and `text_edit_singleline` expanded to 180+ px). Consequently, column horizontal positions drifted independently on every row. Furthermore, in Data View the headers were placed inside the virtualized `show_rows` callback, causing them to drift down when scrolling vertically.\n2. **Deterministic Geometric Lock:** Every cell in Data View and Variable View now allocates exact width via `ui.allocate_exact_size` with zero item spacing (`item_spacing = (0, 0)`). Backgrounds, crisp borders, and clipped text rendering (`with_clip_rect`) guarantee mathematical sub-pixel alignment between header columns and all row cells across the entire dataset.\n3. **Two-Axis Scrolling with Sticky Headers:** Implemented classic spreadsheet ergonomics (SPSS / Excel): an outer `ScrollArea::horizontal()` scrolls both the header row and table body synchronously along the X axis, while an inner `ScrollArea::vertical()` handles vertical virtualization. Column headers stay pinned at the top of the viewport and never scroll out of view.\n4. **Constrained Interactive Widgets:** In Variable View, the `TextEdit` single-line widget and the `ComboBox` measure selector are strictly bounded within their cell rects via `allocate_new_ui` with `UiBuilder`, preventing adjacent columns from being displaced.\n5. **Verification:** All 38 workspace tests passing with `-j 1`, `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` 100% clean, `xtask layers` verified, and `cargo fmt` applied."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751059300",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "---"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751060200",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Phase 2: L2 Mathematical Engine statcraft_algo, Descriptives Dialog & Pivot Tables"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1794063483751060600",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "*Time: October 27, 2026, 18:20 (~20 minutes)*"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751061400",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Established the second computational layer of the StatCraft architecture — the statistical procedure engine:\n1. **L2 Mathematical Algorithms (`statcraft_algo`):**\n   - Implemented `compute_descriptives`: valid/missing observations $N$, mean $\\bar{x}$, standard error of mean $SE_{mean}$, unbiased sample variance $s^2$, sample standard deviation $s$, minimum, maximum, range, sum, unbiased Fisher-Pearson sample skewness $G_1$ (with $SE_{skew}$) and Fisher excess kurtosis $G_2$ (with $SE_{kurt}$).\n   - Implemented categorical frequency distributions `compute_frequencies` (frequencies, total percent, valid percent, cumulative percent).\n   - **Golden Oracle Testing:** Rigorous mathematical unit tests verified against Python `scipy.stats` reference values with precision $\\le 10^{-6}$.\n   - **Never Crash Principle:** Comprehensive edge-case handling for empty vectors, single-item samples, NaN sequences, and missing codes without panics.\n2. **L5 Command Bus (`statcraft_syntax`):**\n   - Implemented typed `DescriptivesCommand` (`stat.descriptives`) with JSON parameter specifications for AI agents.\n   - Built SPSS syntax emitter generating `DESCRIPTIVES VARIABLES=... /STATISTICS=MEAN STDDEV MIN MAX.`.\n3. **L6 Variable Picker Dialog and Pivot Table (`statcraft_app`):**\n   - Implemented `Analyze > Descriptive Statistics > Descriptives...` modal conforming to SPSS desktop UX: source and target variable lists with vector measure badges, vector chevron transfer buttons `[ > ]` and `[ < ]`, statistics selection checkboxes, action buttons (`OK`, `Paste`, `Reset`, `Cancel`).\n   - Integrated formatted SPSS-style Pivot Table inside Output Viewer with numerical formatting and authentic grid themes.\n4. **DoD Compliance:**\n   - Architecture verified with `cargo xtask layers`.\n   - All 47 workspace tests passing (`cargo test --workspace -j 1`).\n   - Localization linter `i18n_lint_test` verifies zero hardcoded strings across all new dialogs and menus.\n   - `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` and `cargo fmt` 100% clean."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751069700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "---"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751070600",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Phase 2.1: Dialog Layout and Pivot Table Row Alignment Fix"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1794063483751071000",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "*Time: October 27, 2026, 18:35 (~15 minutes)*"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751071700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Fixed two critical UI layout defects discovered during visual testing:\n1. **Compact Centered Variable Picker Dialog:**\n   - Resolved window width runaway across the screen by constraining `Window` size ($500 \\times 420$ px) and anchoring to viewport center (`Align2::CENTER_CENTER`).\n   - Fixed variable source/target list dimensions ($196 \\times 150$ px) so transfer buttons `[ > ]` and `[ < ]` stay centered between panels.\n   - Resolved egui `ScrollArea ID 4DF5` collisions using distinct `id_salt` tokens.\n   - Added instant double-click item transfer between variable lists.\n2. **Vertical Row Flow in Output Viewer:**\n   - Root cause of the endless horizontal line: `ScrollArea` inside the detail panel inherited `Direction::LeftToRight` from parent `ui.horizontal`. Table headers and all observation rows (`age`, `gender`, `education`) were rendered side-by-side on a single endless row.\n   - Converted detail panel to strict vertical flow (`ui.vertical`). Each variable is now placed on its own row, stacked vertically under the table header.\n   - Added standard SPSS `Valid N (listwise)` footer summary row.\n3. **Verification:** All 47 workspace tests green (`cargo test --workspace -j 1`), Clippy and Fmt clean, release executable built."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751073500",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "---"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751074200",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Phase 2.2: Full Dock Height in Output Viewer & Elimination of Slit Scrolling"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1794063483751074600",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "*Time: October 27, 2026, 18:45 (~15 minutes)*"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751075400",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Resolved layout height collapse causing the output viewer reports area to shrink to ~80 px:\n1. **Defect Root Cause:** `ui.horizontal` was previously used to divide the left outline tree from the right pivot table viewing panel. In `egui`, horizontal rows shrink-wrap their cross-axis bounding box to the smallest child item (the collapsed single-item outline tree header, $\\sim 60-80$ px). The inner `ScrollArea` of the report viewer was clamped to this slit, forcing the user to scroll vertically to see each table row.\n2. **Explicit Tab Rectangle Splitting:** Replaced `ui.horizontal` with explicit geometric bounding box subdivision of the dock tab (`full_rect = ui.available_rect_before_wrap()`):\n   - Left outline navigation panel receives `left_rect` with fixed 180 px width and 100% tab height (`full_rect.height()`);\n   - Clean vertical separator stroke between panels;\n   - Right detail panel receives `right_rect` claiming all remaining width and 100% tab height via `ui.allocate_new_ui(UiBuilder::new().max_rect(right_rect))`.\n3. **Outcome:** Pivot tables and logs now render freely down the entire screen height as a continuous readable statistical document.\n4. **Verification:** All 48 workspace tests green (`cargo test --workspace -j 1`), Clippy and Fmt clean, layers verified with `cargo xtask layers`, release binary compiled."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751077100",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "---"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751078200",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Phase 3: Frequency Analysis, Variable Metadata Dictionary (Value Labels / Missing Values), and SPSS Tables"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1794063483751078600",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "*Time: October 27, 2026, 19:30 (~25 minutes)*"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751079100",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Implemented the third core milestone of the StatCraft roadmap — the Frequencies procedure and the complete interactive variable metadata lifecycle:\n1. **L2 Mathematical Engine (`statcraft_algo`):**\n   - Extended the `compute_frequencies_detailed` procedure with comprehensive metadata integration (value labels, discrete missing values, range missing values).\n   - Implemented percentiles and quartiles ($Q_1 = 25\\%$, $Q_2 = 50\\%$ Median, $Q_3 = 75\\%$) conforming to the standard SPSS HAVERAGE definition (Weibull / Type 6: $r = p(n+1)$).\n   - Deterministic numeric/lexical category sorting and calculation of frequency counts, total %, valid %, and cumulative %.\n2. **L5 Command Bus (`statcraft_syntax`):**\n   - Created typed `FrequenciesCommand` (`stat.frequencies`) with JSON parameter specs for AI agents and SPSS syntax generator `FREQUENCIES VARIABLES=... /STATISTICS=STDDEV MEAN MEDIAN /ORDER=ANALYSIS.`.\n   - Created metadata mutation commands `VarSetValueLabelsCommand` (`var.set_value_labels`) and `VarSetMissingValuesCommand` (`var.set_missing_values`) with full Undo/Redo.\n   - Registered all commands in `CommandBus::with_defaults()`.\n3. **L6 Interactive Dialogs & Presentation (`statcraft_app`):**\n   - **Frequencies Dialog (`FrequenciesDialog`):** Centered modal ($500 \\times 420$ px) with source/target variable lists, vector transfer arrows `[ > ]` and `[ < ]`, instant double-click item transfer, \"Display frequency tables\" toggle, and action buttons (`OK`, `Paste`, `Reset`, `Cancel`).\n   - **Value Labels Dialog (`ValueLabelsDialog`):** Modal for adding, updating, and removing `Code -> Label` mappings with scrollable list and selection.\n   - **Missing Values Dialog (`MissingValuesDialog`):** Modal supporting \"No missing values\", \"Discrete missing values\" (up to 3 values), and \"Range plus optional discrete value\".\n   - **Variable View Integration:** Added authentic SPSS-style `[...]` button inside the \"Values\" and \"Missing\" cells, opening the metadata dialogs.\n   - **Data View Integration:** Connected `1/A` toggle button on the toolbar for instant switching between raw codes and value labels.\n   - **Output Viewer:** Rendering genuine SPSS frequency tables displaying `Value/Label`, `Frequency`, `Percent`, `Valid Percent`, `Cumulative Percent`, summary rows (`Total Valid`, `System Missing`, `Total`), and percentiles block.\n4. **Verification & Definition of Done:**\n   - Strict Resource Guard (`-j 1` across all tasks).\n   - 100% of workspace tests passing (`cargo test --workspace -j 1`).\n   - Localization linter `i18n_lint_test` verifies zero hardcoded literals and 100% key parity between `en.ftl` and `ru.ftl`.\n   - Architectural layer linter `cargo run --package xtask -j 1 -- layers` passed cleanly.\n   - `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` and `cargo fmt --check` clean."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751083900",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "---"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751084900",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Phase 4: Full Two-Way Reactive Data and Metadata Editor (Variable View & Data View)"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1794063483751085600",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "*Time: October 27, 2026, 21:05 (~30 minutes)*"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751086300",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Implemented the fourth foundational milestone of StatCraft — a complete two-way reactive data and metadata editor, turning the application from a passive viewer into an interactive statistical spreadsheet:"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751087200",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "1. **\"Blank State\" Out of the Box:**\n   - Launching StatCraft without opening a file now initializes an interactive blank dataset (`DataSet::blank(40, 0)`).\n   - The user is immediately greeted by an editable spreadsheet grid (40 cases) and can start entering data or defining variables right away without placeholder blocks."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751088500",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "2. **Full Canon of 9 SPSS Variable Types & `VariableTypeDialog`:**\n   - On layer L1 `statcraft_core`, the `DataType` enum was expanded to all 9 classical SPSS types: `Numeric`, `Comma`, `Dot`, `Scientific`, `Date`, `Dollar`, `CustomCurrency`, `String`, `RestrictedNumeric`.\n   - Core formatting `get_cell_display` now formats numbers according to type parameters (comma/dot thousand groupings, decimal digits, currency symbols, and zero-padded integer widths).\n   - Core parser `set_cell_parsed` cleanses currency and formatting symbols and normalizes user input into valid numerical or text values.\n   - On L6 `statcraft_app`, built a centered modal dialog `VariableTypeDialog` ($480 \\times 360$ px) featuring 9 radio buttons, dynamic width/decimals inputs, date format selectors (`dd-mmm-yyyy`, `yyyy-mm-dd` etc.), and custom currency selectors (`CCA`..`CCE`)."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751090100",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "3. **Interactive `Variable View`:**\n   - **Name:** In-place borderless `TextEdit` (`.frame(false)`) with identifier validation and uniqueness checks.\n   - **Type:** Shows localized type name plus an authentic `[...]` button opening `VariableTypeDialog`.\n   - **Width & Decimals:** Compact vector spinners with `▲ / ▼` buttons (step 1); decimals are automatically disabled for string variables.\n   - **Label:** In-place singleline text edit for the full human-readable variable label.\n   - **Align & Role:** Click to cycle through values (`Left` $\\to$ `Right` $\\to$ `Center`; `Input` $\\to$ `Target` $\\to$ `Both` $\\to$ `None`).\n   - **Measure:** Click to cycle through `Scale` $\\to$ `Ordinal` $\\to$ `Nominal` with crisp vector icons.\n   - **New Variable Ghost Row (`*`):** An empty row is always available at the bottom; typing a name automatically registers the variable and appends a new column to `Data View`.\n   - **Row Context Menu:** Right-clicking row numbers brings up \"Insert Variable\" and \"Clear / Delete Variable\"."
