      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751526700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Implemented the canonical time-series shift procedure from IBM SPSS Statistics — `Transform -> Shift Values (Lead / Lag)...` (`transform.shift_values` command / `SHIFT VALUES` syntax):\n1. **L2 Algorithmic Foundation (`crates/statcraft_algo/src/shift.rs`):**\n   - Defined `ShiftDirection` enum (`Lag` — shift down referencing past cases, `Lead` — shift up referencing future cases);\n   - Core function `compute_shift_raw(values, direction, step)` over `RawValue` column vectors with arbitrary step $K \\ge 1$;\n   - Full edge-case handling: step $K = 0$ or empty vectors return identical clones; $K \\ge N$ fills the vector with `RawValue::Null`;\n   - For `Lag(step)`, the first $K$ observations are padded with `RawValue::Null`, followed by `values[i - step]`;\n   - For `Lead(step)`, observations are shifted up by $K$ positions, with the trailing $K$ cells filled with `RawValue::Null`;\n   - 100% safe Rust without `unwrap`/`expect`/`panic`, unit tested across empty cases, nulls, and string fields.\n2. **L5 Command Bus & Syntax Translation (`crates/statcraft_syntax/src/commands/shift_values_cmd.rs`):**\n   - Strongly-typed `ShiftValuesCommand` (`transform.shift_values`) registered in `CommandBus`;\n   - JSON parameter `specs()` for AI agents (`source_var`, `target_var`, `direction`, `step`, `target_label`);\n   - Canonical SPSS syntax generator:"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751529000",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "code": "     SHIFT VALUES /VARIABLE=sales /RESULT=sales_lag1 /LAG=1.\n     VARIABLE LABELS sales_lag1 \"Previous Sales\".\n     EXECUTE.",
        "language": "text"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_code_1794063483751530200",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "code"
    },
