      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Prepared and published **StatCraft v0.2.1** for all supported operating systems (Windows, Linux, macOS ARM64/x64). This release consolidates the results of a rigorous evidence-based mathematical audit verifying full parity with the canonical IBM SPSS Statistics 24 algorithms, alongside finalization of the Transform procedures:"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751687800",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "1. **Clean-Room Mathematical Audit via Craft Anything:**\n   * Utilized the open-source MCP engine **[Craft Anything](https://github.com/storytold/craft-anything)** in strict `clean-room: true` mode to verify each mathematical formula in `statcraft_algo` against the *IBM SPSS Statistics 24 Algorithms Guide* (1,271 pp.);\n   * Published synchronized bilingual audit documentation: primary English guide [`docs/SPSS_ALGORITHMS_AUDIT.md`](SPSS_ALGORITHMS_AUDIT.md) and Russian mirror [`docs/SPSS_ALGORITHMS_AUDIT_RU.md`](SPSS_ALGORITHMS_AUDIT_RU.md) with header language switches;\n   * Verified 100% formula equivalence with Golden Oracle precision $\\le 10^{-6}$ across all 5 procedure blocks:\n     1. *Descriptives & Basic Statistics:* Spicer provisional moments, Bliss sample kurtosis, HAVERAGE quartiles, Yates correction, Pearson $\\chi^2$, Fisher's exact test, ANOVA $\\eta^2$;\n     2. *Mean Comparisons:* Mean-centered Levene test, Student's $t$, Welch's $t$ with Satterthwaite fractional $df$, paired $t$-test, One-Way ANOVA;\n     3. *Associations & Multivariates:* Pearson, Spearman, Kendall $\\tau_b$ with full tie adjustments, OLS/WLS regression, Tolerance/VIF, cyclic Jacobi eigensolver for PCA, Bartlett sphericity, KMO measure, Cronbach's $\\alpha$;\n     4. *Nonparametric Tests:* Mann-Whitney $U$, Wilcoxon $W$, Kruskal-Wallis $H_{adj}$, Wilcoxon signed-rank test with tie-corrected variance, exact binomial Sign test;\n     5. *Data Transformations:* Blom, Tukey, Rankit, Van der Waerden normal proportions, Acklam inverse normal CDF, MDLP entropy discretization (Fayyad & Irani), linear interpolation and trend."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751689300",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "2. **Finalization of the Data Transformation Suite (`Transform`):**\n   * Production activation of Automated Data Preparation (`adp`) and Programmability Transformations (`programmability`), removing all `[dev]` badges;\n   * 100% coverage of the Transform menu with native DialogKit modal interfaces and Output Viewer pivot tables."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751690400",
