    {
      "data": {
        "text": "*Time: November 2, 2026, 17:30 (~50 minutes)*"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751693600",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Executed a rigorous, line-by-line instrumental Clean-Room audit of the `statcraft_algo` core and `statcraft_syntax` command bus against the *IBM SPSS Statistics 24 Algorithms Guide* (1,271 pp.), recording full evidentiary proof into **Craft Anything MCP** (`hyp_1` through `hyp_15`):"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751694400",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "1. **Block 7: Mathematical Expressions & Evaluator (COMPUTE & expr_eval):**\n   * **Identified Divergences from IBM SPSS Canon:**\n     1. *Exponentiation vs Unary Minus Precedence:* in SPSS, `**` binds tighter than unary minus (`-2**2 = -4`). In `parser.rs`, unary minus holds precedence 7 against 6 for exponentiation, yielding `(-2)**2 = +4`;\n     2. *Logical NOT Precedence:* in SPSS, `NOT` is evaluated after relational operators (`NOT a = b` $\\to$ `NOT (a = b)`). In `parser.rs`, `NOT` holds precedence 7 (above relational operators at 3), erroneously parsing as `(NOT a) = b`;\n     3. *Kleene 3-Valued Logic (3VL):* in `mod.rs`, any `NaN` unconditionally short-circuits to `NaN` instead of following Kleene 3VL (`TRUE OR MISSING = TRUE`, `FALSE AND MISSING = FALSE`);\n     4. *Functions:* `eval.rs` lacks trigonometric functions `SIN`, `COS`, `TAN`, modulo operator `MOD`, and SPSS alias `LG10`.\n   * **Confirmed:** Dijkstra's Shunting-yard AST parser for basic arithmetic, safe `NaN` and divide-by-zero isolation (`Never Crash`), elementary functions `SQRT`, `EXP`, `LN`, `LOG10`, `ABS`, `RND`, `TRUNC`, and aggregates `SUM`, `MEAN`, `MIN`, `MAX`."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751695800",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "2. **Block 8: Time Series Transformations & Case Shifts (DIFF, SDIFF, SMA, CSUM, LAG, LEAD):**\n   * **Confirmed:** exact formula match for $\\Delta^d X_t$ and $\\Delta_s X_t = X_t - X_{t-s}$, `SYSMIS` cascade in `CSUM`, and shift operators `LAG(k)` and `LEAD(k)` with preservation of underlying data types (`hyp_4`, `hyp_6`, `hyp_7: supported`);\n   * **Identified Divergence:** `SimpleMovingAverage(span)` in `time_series.rs` implements a trailing/prior window (known in SPSS as `PMA` — Prior Moving Average), whereas canonical SPSS `SMA(span)` computes a centered moving average (`hyp_5: refuted`)."
