    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Phase 58: Batch Syntax Engine (.sps) & Clean-Room Evidentiary Audit (Microplans S-01 — S-05)"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1794063483751790200",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "*Time: November 6, 2026, 18:55 (~45 minutes)*"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751790800",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Implemented and audited according to the *IBM SPSS Statistics 24 Command Syntax Reference* a comprehensive batch command syntax parser and dispatcher (**Batch Syntax Engine & Dispatcher**) in `crates/statcraft_syntax`. The engine delivers raw script `.sps` batch execution capabilities via `CommandBus`, activates the desktop `Syntax Editor` toolbar with real-time log echoing and statistical table insertion in `Output Viewer`, and guarantees a 100% reversible round-trip cycle `GUI -> to_sps -> SyntaxParser -> CommandBus`:"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751791700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "1. **Command Block Lexer & Tokenizer (`statcraft_syntax::syntax_parser::lexer`):**\n   * Engineered streaming `SyntaxLexer` splitting script text into `RawCommandBlock` items bounded by command-terminating periods `.`;\n   * Complete isolation of non-terminator periods: decimal fractions in floating-point numbers (`3.14`, `0.95`) and dots inside single (`'path.sav'`) and double (`\"model.v1\"`) quoted strings do not truncate commands;\n   * Full support for quote escaping via doubling (`''` and `\"\"`), with line and column tracking on unclosed string literals;\n   * Recognition of comments beginning with `*` or the keyword `COMMENT` spanning until the terminating period."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751793100",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "2. **Subcommand & Variable Range Parser (`statcraft_syntax::syntax_parser::parser`):**\n   * Detection of compound command names (`SORT CASES`, `SPLIT FILE`);\n   * Structured parsing of subcommands with leading slash `/` and positional clauses;\n   * Parenthesized parameter tokenization (`GROUPS=gender(1 2)`, `CI(0.95)`, `salary (D)`);\n   * Automatic expansion of variable ranges `VAR1 TO VAR5` matching sequential column order in active dataset `VariableDictionary`;\n   * Expansion of the keyword `ALL` into all active dataset variables."
      },
