      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Implemented the new **`statcraft_bridge`** crate and integrated it into the StatCraft desktop GUI following the **Code Mode** paradigm (compact, high-level executable interface instead of classic bloated MCP micro-tools):"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751825300",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "1. **Code Mode Philosophy & `statcraft_bridge` Crate:**\n   - Designed a streamlined suite of 6 high-level tools:\n     1. `statcraft_run_syntax`: core Code Mode execution engine for batch SPSS syntax scripts (`.sps`) handling data creation (`DATA LIST`), transforms (`COMPUTE`, `RECODE`), dictionary metadata (`VARIABLE LEVEL`, `VALUE LABELS`, `MISSING VALUES`), and full statistical analysis (`FREQUENCIES`, `DESCRIPTIVES`, `CROSSTABS`, `T-TEST`, `ONEWAY`, `REGRESSION`, `RELIABILITY`);\n     2. `statcraft_load_dataset`: direct injection of raw tabular data (CSV/TSV text) into active memory without intermediate disk files;\n     3. `statcraft_list_variables`: inspection of variable dictionary metadata (measures, types, labels, missing values);\n     4. `statcraft_get_data_preview`: preview sample of the first $N$ rows for rapid distribution checks;\n     5. `statcraft_insert_output_note`: insertion of formatted analytical findings and scientific conclusion cards into the Output Viewer tree;\n     6. `statcraft_set_active_tab`: intentional tab switching (`data`, `variable`, `output`, `syntax`) without stealing user focus.\n   - JSON-RPC 2.0 wire protocol over local TCP socket `127.0.0.1:18493` (Loopback);\n   - Non-blocking socket listener with clean `AtomicBool` exit and guaranteed socket liberation upon `Drop`."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751827200",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "2. **Long-Running Service in App (`statcraft_app::bridge_service`):**\n   - Dedicated `BridgeService` managing the server lifecycle within `StatCraftApp`;\n   - Inter-thread channels (`BridgeAppRequest` and `oneshot` responders) bridging the TCP server thread to the UI frame loop in `update()`;\n   - Direct execution via `syntax_runner::run_syntax_batch` and `DataSet::from_raw_table`;\n   - In-memory ring buffer `BridgeLogRing` holding up to 100 entries with zero disk footprint."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751828600",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "3. **Interactive Semantic Activity Log & Dialog (`dialogs/mcp_bridge_dialog`):**\n   - Modular dialog built on canonical `DialogKit` (`DialogShell::standard`, `GroupBox`, `SubdialogActionBar`);\n   - 100% vector-first UI: circular status indicator (`ui.painter().circle_filled`) with dynamic colors (emerald green / amber / gray) and zero Unicode tofu emojis;\n   - One-click copy buttons for MCP configuration and agent Skill prompts;\n   - Semantic live activity log: stores typed `BridgeLogEvent` variants, enabling on-the-fly bilingual translation of historical log entries via Fluent catalogs (`en.ftl` / `ru.ftl`)."
