      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Delivered a comprehensive architectural modernization of the StatCraft Socket Bridge (Bridge v2), transforming the bridge interface into an **autonomous Code Mode (SPSS Syntax REPL)**. External AI agents (Claude, Antigravity, local LLMs) are now 100% self-sufficient without access to Rust source code or manual documentation:"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751834400",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "1. **Closing the Feedback Loop (Code Mode REPL Output Return):**\n   - Extended the batch syntax execution engine `syntax_runner::run_syntax_batch` with `SyntaxBatchOutcome { count: usize, output_text: String }`;\n   - Formatted all newly created procedures (SPSS Pivot Tables: ANOVA, Descriptives, Frequencies, T-Tests, Regression, Reliability) into clean monospace ASCII tables via `export_procedures_to_txt` and returned them directly in the text body of `statcraft_run_syntax`;\n   - External agents immediately receive exact sample sizes, means, standard errors, Student's $t$ and Fisher's $F$ statistics, exact $p$-values, and confidence intervals in their conversation context."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751835700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "2. **Dynamic Self-Documentation & MCP Resources (Zero-Manual-Docs):**\n   - Implemented syntax commands `HELP.` (general catalog of analytical procedure categories) and `HELP <COMMAND>.` (canonical syntax template, subcommands, and usage examples, e.g. `HELP ONEWAY.`);\n   - Registered `HelpCommand` (`util.help`) in `CommandBus`, making syntax help accessible through both the parser and direct command execution;\n   - Added native MCP Resources support to the stdio bridge server (`statcraft.exe --mcp`):\n     - `resources/list`: exposes dynamic resource descriptor `statcraft://syntax-reference`;\n     - `resources/read`: dynamically compiles comprehensive syntax and procedure manuals via `statcraft_syntax::generate_full_syntax_reference()` directly from the binary;\n   - Intelligent Self-Correction: when encountering an unknown command or typo, the parser evaluates Levenshtein distance against known commands and suggests the closest valid procedure (`Did you mean 'ONEWAY'? Type 'HELP.' for available commands.`)."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751837300",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "3. **SPSS Variable Dictionary Syntax Mappers (`variables.rs`):**\n   - Implemented syntax mappers for dataset variable metadata management:\n     - `VARIABLE LEVEL varlist (SCALE | ORDINAL | NOMINAL).` -> `\"var.set_measure\"`;\n     - `VARIABLE LABELS var 'Label'.` -> `\"var.set_label\"`;\n     - `VALUE LABELS var code 'Label'.` -> `\"var.set_value_labels\"`;\n     - `MISSING VALUES var (val1, val2) | (low THRU high).` -> `\"var.set_missing_values\"`;\n   - Upgraded core commands `SetMeasureCommand`, `SetLabelCommand`, `VarSetValueLabelsCommand`, and `VarSetMissingValuesCommand` to accept variable names (`var_name`, `variables`, `assignments`) alongside column indices."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751838800",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "4. **Statistical Procedure Mapping Fixes:**\n   - `ONEWAY`: aligned parameter keys with canonical `OneWayAnovaCommand` schema (`dependent_vars`, top-level `descriptives`, `homogeneity`, `ci`);\n   - `RELIABILITY`: aligned variable list key with `variables`;\n   - `FACTOR`: aligned variable list key with `variables`;\n   - `MEANS`: lifted summary options (`cell_mean`, `cell_count`, `cell_stddev`, `anova`) to top-level command arguments."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751839900",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "5. **Quality Control & Definition of Done:**\n   - 100% test pass across the workspace via `cargo test --workspace -j 1` (0 failures, 0 regressions);\n   - New integration test suites: `syntax_bridge_v2_tests.rs` and `syntax_runner_and_output_tests.rs`;\n   - Static linters and architectural guards: `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- layers`, `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- file-guard` (294 files strictly within limits), `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- design-guard`, `cargo fmt --check`;\n   - Zero-warning compiler policy: `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` (0 warnings);\n   - Refactored agent skill `.agents/skills/statcraft-assistant/SKILL.md` to guide agents toward autonomous Code Mode REPL workflows."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751841800",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
