      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Phase 63: Self-Sufficient Introspective Bridge Engine & Universal Code Mode (Zero-Maintenance Introspective Bridge)"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1794063483751843200",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "*Time: November 7, 2026, 15:05 (~35 minutes)*"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1794063483751844000",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Eliminated the architectural bottleneck of manual command registry maintenance and hardcoded procedure matchers in the socket bridge and output runner. Established the core principle of **\"Write Once — Works for All Future Functions\"**:\n1. **Live Runtime Introspection from Compiled Binary (Zero-Code Base Discovery):**\n   - Extended `CommandBus::list_specs()` with categories and syntax keywords, generating a dynamic live catalog of all engine commands registered in the core;\n   - Added `statcraft_list_commands` tool and `statcraft://commands` dynamic resource to `statcraft_bridge`: external agents receive the exact catalog of all available procedures and JSON parameter schemas on the fly, eliminating the need to read or guess the codebase;\n   - Added `CommandBus::find_by_syntax_keyword` for dynamic command resolution.\n2. **Universal Code Mode (`statcraft_execute_command` & `RUN COMMAND` Directive):**\n   - Added universal execution tool `statcraft_execute_command` to the MCP bridge and IPC protocol: agents can invoke any engine command by `command_id` and JSON arguments with automatic parameter validation;\n   - Added universal syntax directive in `SyntaxParser` and `SyntaxDispatcher`:\n     `RUN COMMAND \"<command_id>\" { <json_params> }.` (with `CALL \"<command_id>\" { ... }.` alias);\n   - Every newly registered `EngineCommand` becomes instantly executable both directly through MCP and inside batch `.sps` syntax scripts without requiring dedicated syntax mappers.\n3. **Universal Output Viewer Renderer (Zero-Match Fallback):**\n   - Replaced hardcoded `match parsed.name.as_str()` in `syntax_runner.rs` with an open two-tier rendering model;\n   - Introduced `OutputItemKind::GenericReport` and isolated rendering module `tables_generic.rs`: arbitrary command results are automatically formatted into SPSS-styled summary tables and key-value cards, recorded into the `OutputViewer` tree, and streamed to `output_text` in bridge responses;\n   - Synchronously updated Fluent localization catalogs `locales/en.ftl` and `locales/ru.ftl` with `output-generic-title` and `output-table`.\n4. **Quality Control & Definition of Done:**\n   - 100% test pass across the workspace via `cargo test --workspace -j 1` (0 failures, 0 regressions);\n   - Full pass of dialog and output viewer invariant suites: `cargo test -p statcraft_app --test dialog_invariants -j 1` and `output_viewer_invariants -j 1`;\n   - Architecture and code guard verifications: `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- layers`, `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- file-guard` (295 files strictly within size limits), `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- design-guard`, and `cargo fmt --check`;\n   - Strict compiler and linting gate: `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` (0 warnings);\n   - Localization linter pass: `cargo test -p statcraft_i18n -j 1` (4/4 passed)."
