idden UI regressions:<br>1. **Tooling Guard (`xtask/src/file_guard.rs`):**<br>   - Implemented and integrated the source linter `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- file-guard` with differentiated thresholds:<br>     * Leaf functional modules (`algo/`, `syntax/commands/`, `dialogs/`, `views/output_view/`): strict limit of **500 lines**;<br>     * Complex interactive editors (`data_view.rs`, `variable_view.rs`, `syntax_editor.rs`): limit of **1000 lines**;<br>     * Root application coordinator (`app.rs`): ceiling of **1500 lines**;<br>     * General modules: limit of **1000 lines**;<br>   - Instructive error message on threshold violation: categorically forbids truncating columns/features or compressing code into one-liners, mandating architectural decomposition instead (&quot;Decompose, Don&#39;t Cut&quot; principle).<br>2. **Architectural Decomposition of Tables and Models (`output_view/`):**<br>   - Decomposed monolithic `tables_ttest.rs` (571 lines) into three focused modules:<br>     * `tables_ttest_onesample.rs` (127 lines): One-Sample Statistics and One-Sample Test tables + TSV;<br>     * `tables_ttest_indep.rs` (180 lines): two-tier Group Statistics and Independent Samples Test (Levene + Welch/Student) tables + TSV;<br>     * `tables_ttest_paired.rs` (204 lines): Paired Statistics, Correlations, and Paired Differences tables + TSV;<br>     * `tables_common.rs` (90 lines): reusable layout and cell painting utilities;<br>   - Decomposed `model.rs` (616 lines) into clean data structures (`model.rs`, 175 lines) and procedure builder methods (`builder.rs`, 456 lines);<br>   - Extracted subdialog `ttest_indep_define_groups.rs` (46 lines) from `ttest_indep_dialog.rs` (462 lines);<br>   - Extracted format commands `var_format_cmds.rs` (270 lines) from `var_cmds.rs` (294 lines);<br>   - Result: 100% of workspace files comply with size limits (76 files scanned).<br>3. **UI Invariants Test Suite (`crates/statcraft_app/tests/output_viewer_invariants.rs`):**<br>   - Created headless UI integration tests eliminating the risk of accidental feature erasure:<br>     1. `test_continuous_history_accumulation`: verifies continuous retention of all analyses (Descriptives, Frequencies, 3 t-tests, ANOVA), strictly monotonic procedure IDs, and preservation of prior Notes/Log blocks;<br>     2. `test_exhaustive_enum_payloads_render_without_panics`: headless rendering of all 11 `OutputItemKind` variants in `egui` (including edge cases: zero degrees of freedom, empty lists, zero variance) guaranteeing 0 panics;<br>     3. `test_tsv_export_golden_headers`: verifies exact golden TSV structures (presence of `Mean`, `Std. Deviation`, `Valid N (listwise)`, `Valid Percent`, `Total`, `Levene`, `Equal variances assumed / not assumed`, `Paired Differences`, `Between Groups`, `Sum of Squares`, `F`, `Sig.`);<br>     4. `test_outline_tree_navigation_integrity`: verifies synchronization between Outline tree focus and procedure scroll, and item deletion integrity.<br>4. **Normative Grounding (`AGENTS.md`):**<br>   - Added Section 12 &quot;File Size Guard &amp; Feature Retention&quot; to the general development regulations (`AGENTS.md` and `.agents/rules/AGENTS.md`);<br>   - Integrated `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- file-guard` and `cargo test -p statcraft_app --test output_viewer_invariants -j 1` as mandatory Definition of Done (DoD) criteria.<br>5. **Quality &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - Source linter `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- file-guard` — 76 files scanned, 0 violations;<br>   - Invariant tests `output_viewer_invariants` — 4/4 passed;<br>   - Workspace tests `cargo test --workspace -j 1` — 100% passed;<br>   - Layer architecture verified: `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- layers` — 0 violations;<br>   - Parity catalog verified: `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- parity` — clean;<br>   - Localization linter `i18n_lint_test` — 3/3 passed;<br>   - Pure compiler cleanliness: `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` — 0 errors, 0 warnings;<br>   - Clean release build: `cargo build --package statcraft_app --release -j 1` — succeeded (1m 12s).</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 6.6: DialogKit Design System Standardization &amp; Design Guard</h3><p>*Time: October 28, 2026, 16:05 (~40 minutes)*</p><p>Eliminated long-standing visual and architectural dialog inconsistencies: mismatched sizes (`500x380`, `500x420`, `520x440`), shifting action buttons lacking a fixed layout grid, and ad-hoc variable transfer widgets were replaced by the canonical IBM SPSS Statistics design system backed by automated static linting:<br>1. **Canonical Design Specification (`docs/DESIGN_GUIDE.md`):**<br>   - Formalized 4 core StatCraft dialog archetypes: Type 1 (Statistical Procedure, $560 \times 430$ px), Type 2 (Subdialog/Options, $360 \times 300$ px), Type 3 (Properties, $460 \times 380$ px), Type 4 (Compute, $620 \times 480$ px);<br>   - Standardized layout grid, spacing (padding $12$ px, gap $8$/$12$ px), and typography;<br>   - Established the **`i18n Shield`** adaptability rule: uniform action bar button width with padding $\ge 10$ px, preventing layout shifts across language switches (RU $\leftrightarrow$ EN).<br>2. **`DialogKit` Component Library (`crates/statcraft_app/src/dialogs/common/`):**<br>   - `DialogShell`: universal modal window wrapper with standardized dimensions, viewport centering, and modal isolation;<br>   - `TransferButton`: adaptive vector transfer button ($28 \times 28$ px, $3$ px corner radius), automatically orienting the arrow (`-&gt;` / `&lt;-`) towards the active target list;<br>   - `VariablePicker`: two-pane variable list with vector measurement scale icons and canonical `Label [Name]` formatting;<br>   - `DialogActionBar`: Type 1 bottom action bar (`[ OK ] [ Paste ] [ Reset ] [ Cancel ] [ Help ]`) with uniform button widths ($\ge 80 \times 26$ px, $3$ px corner radius);<br>   - `SubdialogActionBar`: bottom action bar for modal subdialogs (`[ Continue ] [ Cancel ] [ Help ]`);<br>   - `SubdialogSidebar`: right vertical action strip for SPS