br>   - Made passing `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- design-guard` and `cargo test -p statcraft_app --test dialog_invariants -j 1` mandatory for Definition of Done (DoD).<br>7. **Quality &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- design-guard` — 0 violations;<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- file-guard` — 86 files scanned, 0 file size violations;<br>   - Invariant tests `dialog_invariants` — 9/9 passed;<br>   - All workspace tests `cargo test --workspace -j 1` — 93 passed (100%);<br>   - Architectural layers `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- layers` — 0 violations;<br>   - Parity catalog `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- parity` — clean;<br>   - Localization linter `i18n_lint_test` — 3/3 passed;<br>   - `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` — 0 warnings;<br>   - `cargo fmt --check` — clean;<br>   - Clean release build `cargo build --package statcraft_app --release -j 1` — succeeded (1m 14s).</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 6.7: Hybrid Localization System — Embedded Catalogs and Dynamic External .ftl Discovery</h3><p>*Time: October 28, 2026, 18:45 (~25 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented a hybrid internationalization (i18n) architecture blending the canonical single-binary portability of the ArtCraft ecosystem with the flexibility of user-contributed translations:<br>1. **Guaranteed Base (Zero-Dependency Single Binary):**<br>   - Official `ru.ftl` and `en.ftl` catalogs remain embedded in the executable via `include_str!`. StatCraft is 100% self-contained, launches from any location, and never fails when external folders are missing.<br>2. **Dynamic Locale Discovery (`discover_and_load_locales`):**<br>   - On startup, the engine scans external paths: `STATCRAFT_LOCALES_DIR` environment variable, `locales/` directory adjacent to the binary (`current_exe()`), and the working `./locales` directory.<br>   - Any discovered `.ftl` file (e.g. `de.ftl`, `es.ftl`, `fr.ftl`) is registered at runtime and immediately surfaces in the `View -&gt; Language` menu without recompiling the application.<br>3. **Seamless Key Overriding (Resource Overriding):**<br>   - When a user supplies an existing language file (e.g. custom `ru.ftl`), external keys override defaults via `add_resource_overriding` without losing untranslated embedded strings.<br>4. **Intelligent Language Display Name (`language_name`):**<br>   - Native autonym is read from the language bundle itself (`lang-name-{lang}` or `lang-name`, e.g. `Deutsch`, `Español`);<br>   - Falls back to active language / English translation;<br>   - Final fallback displays the uppercase language code (`DE`, `ES`). Completely prevents raw keys such as `[lang-name-xx]`.<br>5. **Release Workflow Automation (`.github/workflows/release.yml`):**<br>   - Windows release ZIP `statcraft-windows-x64.zip` now packages the `locales/` directory alongside `statcraft_app.exe`.<br>6. **Testing &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - Authored end-to-end integration test `crates/statcraft_app/tests/i18n_external_locales_test.rs`;<br>   - Added 4 new unit tests in `crates/statcraft_i18n/src/lib.rs`;<br>   - Full test and static analysis pass via `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci` (`ALL CI QUALITY GATES PASSED!`);<br>   - Clean release build `cargo build --package statcraft_app --release -j 1` succeeded in 1m 08s.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 7.1: Contingency Tables (Crosstabs) and Pearson&#39;s Chi-Square Test of Independence ($\chi^2$)</h3><p>*Time: October 28, 2026, 20:55 (~35 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented the fundamental procedure for analyzing categorical and discrete relationships — **Contingency Tables** (*Crosstabs*), association measures, and Pearson&#39;s Chi-Square Test of Independence ($\chi^2$, menu item `Analyze -&gt; Descriptive Statistics -&gt; Crosstabs...`):<br>1. **Mathematical Core L2 (`statcraft_algo::crosstabs` &amp; `crosstabs_types`):**<br>   - Construction of categorical $R \times C$ cross-classification grid supporting string categories and numeric value labels;<br>   - Computation of observed frequencies ($O_{ij}$), expected frequencies ($E_{ij} = \frac{R_i \cdot C_j}{N}$), residuals ($O_{ij} - E_{ij}$), and cell percentage breakdowns (row %, column %, and % of total table);<br>   - Pearson Chi-Square test: $\chi^2 = \sum \frac{(O_{ij} - E_{ij})^2}{E_{ij}}$ with degrees of freedom $df = (R - 1)(C - 1)$;<br>   - Likelihood Ratio test ($G^2$): $2 \sum O_{ij} \ln(O_{ij} / E_{ij})$ for cells with $O_{ij} &gt; 0$;<br>   - Double-precision $p$-value computation of the $\chi^2$ distribution survival function via regularized upper incomplete gamma function $Q(a, x)$ without external dependencies and with zero panics;<br>   - For $2 \times 2$ fourfold tables:<br>     * Yates&#39; Continuity Correction: $\chi^2_{Yates} = \frac{N (|ad - bc| - N/2)^2}{(a+b)(c+d)(a+c)(b+d)}$;<br>     * Two-sided Fisher&#39;s Exact Test computing exact hypergeometric probabilities via log-gamma functions and summing extreme outcomes $P(k) \le P(a) + 10^{-11}$;<br>   - Symmetric measures of association: $\phi = \sqrt{\chi^2 / N}$ and Cramér&#39;s $V$ with approximate asymptotic significance;<br>   - **Golden Oracle:** Unit test verification comparing contingency tables and test statistics against Python `scipy.stats` (`chi2_contingency`, `fisher_exact`) with precision $\le 10^{-6}$.<br>2. **Command Bus &amp; Syntax L5 (`statcraft_syntax::commands::crosstabs_cmd`):**<br>   - Typed engine command `CrosstabsCommand` (`stat.crosstabs`) equipped with JSON parameter specs for external AI agents;<br>   - Generates authentic IBM SPSS syntax:</p><p><em>[code block — open in CapsuleCraft web for its canvas]</em></p><p>3. **User Interface L6 (`statcraft_app::dialogs::crosstabs_dialog`):**<br>   - Fully unified `CrosstabsDialog` ($560 \times 430$ px) built exclusively with `DialogKit` design primitives:<br>     * Source variables picker (`VariablePicker`) on the left;<br>     * Target `Row(s)` and `Column(s)` list pickers in the center with vector `TransferButton`;<br>     * Right sidebar (`SubdialogSidebar`) hosting `[ Cells... ]` and `[ Statistics... ]` subdialog buttons;<br>     * Modal subdialogs for `Cells` (Counts: Observed, Expected, Residuals; Percentages: Row, Column, Total) and `Statistics` (Chi-square, Phi and Cramér&#39;s V) using `SubdialogActionBar`;<br>     * Canonical bottom action bar `DialogActionBar` (`[ OK ] [ Paste ] [ Reset ] [ Cancel ] [ Help ]`).<br>4. **Architectural Coordinator Decomposition (`app_dialogs.rs`):**<br>   - Extracted all modal dialog rendering and execution dispatching out of `app.rs` into `app_dialogs.rs`;<br>   - Reduced `app.rs` from 1485 lines down to 1138 lines, safely below the 1500-line architectural ceiling.<br>5. **Output Viewer Representation (`tables_crosstabs.rs`):**<br>   - Four authentic SPSS Pivot Tables:<br>     1. **Case Processing Summary:** valid, missing, total cases and percentages;<br>     2. **Crosstabulation Table:** multi-tier $R \times C$ matrix displaying all selected cell layers, row totals, and column totals;<br>     3. **Chi-Square Tests:** Pearson Chi-Square, Continuity Correction, Likelihood Ratio, Fisher&#39;s Exact Test, N of Valid Cases;<br>     4. **Symmetric Measures:** Phi, Cramér&#39;s V, and approximate significance;<br>   - TSV clipboard export for spreadsheet workflows and Outline Pane navigation.<br>6. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - Full automated CI gate passed (`cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci` — 100% OK);<br>   - All 96 workspace tests completed with 0 failures;<br>   - Static linters `design-guard`, `file-guard`, `layers`, and `parity` reporting 0 violations;<br>   - Compiler linter `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -j 1 -- -D warnings` — 0 warnings;<br>   - Format validation `cargo fmt --check` — completely clean.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 7.3: Nonparametric Tests for Two Samples (Mann-Whitney $U$ and Wilcoxon $W$)</h3><p>*Time: October 28, 2026, 22:15 (~45 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented the fundamental nonparametric framework for comparing two groups on ordinal scales or non-normally distributed continuous variables — **Two-Independent-Samples Tests** (`Analyze -&gt; Nonparametric Tests -&gt; Two Independent Samples...`):<br>1. **Mathematical Engine L2 (`statcraft_algo::nonparam_twosample` &amp; `nonparam_twosample_types`):**<br>   - Combined ranking algorithm with fractional mid-ranks and tie sum $T = \sum (t_i^3 - t_i)$;<br>   - Calculation of rank sums ($W_1, W_2$) and mean ranks ($\bar{R}_1, \bar{R}_2$) for both groups;<br>   - Mann-Whitney test statistic $U = \min(U_1, U_2)$, where $U_1 = W_1 - \frac{n_1(n_1 + 1)}{2}$;<br>   - Wilcoxon $W$ statistic definition adhering to the IBM SPSS Statistics standard (rank sum of the group with the smaller mean rank);<br>   - Expected value $\mu_U = \frac{n_1 n_2}{2}$ and tie-corrected variance $\sigma_U^2 = \frac{n_1 n_2}{12}\left[ (N + 1) - \frac{\sum (t_i^3 - t_i)}{N(N - 1)} \right]$;<br>   - Asymptotic $Z$-statistic and two-tailed significance derived from the regularized upper incomplete gamma function $Q(0.5, Z^2 / 2)$;<br>   - Wilcoxon Signed-Rank Test for paired observations with ranking of absolute differences $|d_i|$, exclusion of zero-ties, and $W = \min(W^+, W^-)$;<br>   - **Never Crash** protection: graceful handling of small sample sizes ($N &lt; 2$), degenerate zero-variance rank distributions, and flexible numeric/string group codes via `matches_group` on 100% safe Rust;<br>   - **Golden Oracle:** Test suite `nonparam_twosample_tests.rs` validating ranks, $U$, $W$, $Z$, and $p$-value against Python `scipy.stats` (`mannwhitneyu`, `wilcoxon`) and manual SPSS benchmarks with $\le 10^{-6}$ precision.<br>2. **Command Bus &amp; Syntax L5 (`statcraft_syntax::commands::nonparam_twosample_cmd`):**<br>   - Typed engine command `MannWhitneyCommand` (`stat.npar.mann_whitney`) with JSON parameter specs for external AI agents;<br>   - Canonical IBM SPSS Statistics syntax emission:</p><p><em>[code block — open in CapsuleCraft web for its canvas]</em></p><p>3. **User Interface L6 (`statcraft_app::dialogs::nonparam_twosample_dialog`):**<br>   - Modal dialog `Two-Independent-Samples Tests` ($560 \times 430$ px) built with `DialogKit`:<br>     * Source variables list (`VariablePicker`) with scale measurement icons;<br>     * Vector transfer button (`TransferButton`) for test variables and grouping variable;<br>     * Target variables list `Test Variable List:`;<br>     * Selected grouping variable display `Grouping Variable:` with `var(val1 val2)` syntax;<br>     * Right sidebar (`SubdialogSidebar`) with `[ Define Groups... ]` button;<br>     * Modal subdialog `Define Groups` based on `DialogShell::subdialog` with validation of non-empty, non-identical group values;<br>     * `Test Type` group with checkboxes `[x] Mann-Whitney U`, `[ ] Wilcoxon W`, `[ ] Kolmogorov-Smirnov Z`;<br>     * Standard bottom action bar `DialogActionBar` (`[ OK ] [ Paste ] [ Reset ] [ Cancel ] [ Help ]`).<br>4. **Summary Pivot Tables in Output Viewer (`tables_nonparam.rs`):**<br>   - **Ranks Table:** Variable, Group, $N$, Mean Rank, Sum of Ranks, Total row;<br>   - **Test Statistics Table:** Canonical multi-column matrix (Mann-Whitney U, Wilcoxon W, Z, Asymp. Sig. 2-tailed) with grouping variable footnote;<br>   - TSV clipboard export and Outline Pane integration.<br>5. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - Full automated CI gate passed (`cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci` — 100% OK);<br>   - 105 workspace unit and integration tests passing with 0 failures;<br>   - Architectural linters (`design-guard`, `file-guard`, `layers`, `parity`) reporting 0 violations;<br>   - Strict compiler linter `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -j 1 -- -D warnings` — 0 warnings;<br>   - Code formatting `cargo fmt --check` — completely clean.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 7.4: Nonparametric Tests for Two Related Samples (Wilcoxon Signed-Rank Test and Sign Test)</h3><p>*Time: October 29, 2026, 08:15 (~40 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented the fundamental nonparametric framework for paired and repeated-measures analyses when normal distribution of differences is violated — **Two-Related-Samples Tests** (`Analyze -&gt; Nonparametric Tests -&gt; Related Samples (Wilcoxon / Friedman)...`):<br>1. **Mathematical Engine L2 (`statcraft_algo::nonparam_related` &amp; `nonparam_related_types`):**<br>   - Paired difference computation $D_i = Y_i - X_i$ (`var2 - var1`);<br>   - Zero-difference classification as Ties ($D_i = 0$), excluded from ranking per IBM SPSS Statistics standard;<br>   - Sorting and ranking of absolute differences $|D_i|$ with mid-ranks calculation and tie sum $T = \sum (t_j^3 - t_j)$;<br>   - Calculation of negative ($D_i &lt; 0$) and positive ($D_i &gt; 0$) rank sums and mean ranks;<br>   - Tie-corrected variance formula: $\sigma_W^2 = \frac{n(n + 1)(2n + 1)}{24} - \frac{\sum (t_j^3 - t_j)}{48}$;<br>   - Standardized $Z$-statistic with $\pm 0.5$ continuity correction and two-tailed asymptotic significance via regularized incomplete gamma function $Q(0.5, Z^2 / 2)$;<br>   - Dynamic determination of test base (negative vs positive ranks) adhering to SPSS footnote convention;<br>   - **Sign Test:** frequency counts of negative, positive, and zero differences, with exact two-tailed binomial significance calculated via regularized incomplete beta function $I_{0.5}(n - k, k + 1)$;<br>   - **Never Crash** protection: robust handling of zero variance, identical pairs, and missing values on 100% safe Rust;<br>   - **Golden Oracle:** Unit and oracle tests in `nonparam_related_tests.rs` validating ranks, $W$, $Z$, and $p$-value against SciPy and SPSS reference tables with $\le 10^{-6}$ precision.<br>2. **Command Bus &amp; Syntax L5 (`statcraft_syntax::commands::nonparam_related_cmd`):**<br>   - Typed engine command `RelatedSamplesTestCommand` (`stat.npar.related2`) with JSON parameter specs for external AI agents;<br>   - Canonical IBM SPSS Statistics syntax emission:</p><p><em>[code block — open in CapsuleCraft web for its canvas]</em></p><p>3. **User Interface L6 (`statcraft_app::dialogs::nonparam_related_dialog`):**<br>   - Modal dialog `Two-Related-Samples Tests` ($560 \times 430$ px) built with `DialogKit`:<br>     * Source variables list (`VariablePicker`) with scale measurement icons;<br>     * Two-stage slot picker `Current Selections: Variable 1, Variable 2` with adaptive vector transfer buttons;<br>     * Target pairs list `Test Pairs:`;<br>     * `Test Type` group with checkboxes `[x] Wilcoxon`, `[ ] Sign`;<br>     * Standard bottom action bar `DialogActionBar` (`[ OK ] [ Paste ] [ Reset ] [ Cancel ] [ Help ]`).<br>4. **Summary Pivot Tables in Output Viewer (`tables_nonparam_related.rs`):**<br>   - **Ranks Table (Wilcoxon):** Negative Ranks, Positive Ranks, Ties, Total ($N$, Mean Rank, Sum of Ranks) with difference direction footnotes;<br>   - **Test Statistics Table (Wilcoxon):** $Z$-score, Asymp. Sig. (2-tailed), method and rank base footnotes;<br>   - **Frequencies Table (Sign Test):** Negative Differences, Positive Differences, Ties, Total;<br>   - **Test Statistics Table (Sign Test):** Exact Sig. (2-tailed);<br>   - TSV clipboard export and Outline Pane integration.<br>5. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - Full automated CI gate passed (`cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci` — 100% OK);<br>   - All 110+ workspace unit and integration tests passing with 0 failures;<br>   - Differential file size guard verified (`file-guard` $\le 500$ lines for leaf modules);<br>   - Architectural linters (`design-guard`, `layers`, `parity`) reporting 0 violations;<br>   - Synchronous dual-catalog localization (`locales/en.ftl`, `locales/ru.ftl`);<br>   - Strict compiler linter `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -j 1 -- -D warnings` — 0 warnings;<br>   - Code formatting `cargo fmt --check` — completely clean.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 7.2: Bivariate Correlations (Pearson $r$, Spearman $\rho$, Kendall $\tau$-b)</h3><p>*Time: October 28, 2026, 21:30 (~35 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented the fundamental bivariate relationship analysis procedure — **Bivariate Correlations** (`Analyze -&gt; Correlate -&gt; Bivariate...`):<br>1. **Mathematical Engine L2 (`statcraft_algo::correlations` &amp; `correlations_types`):**<br>   - Pearson linear correlation coefficient calculation ($r = \frac{\sum (x_i - \bar{x})(y_i - \bar{y})}{\sqrt{\sum (x_i - \bar{x})^2 \sum (y_i - \bar{y})^2}}$), cross-product sum of squares ($SS_{xy}$), and unbiased sample covariance ($Cov(x, y)$);<br>   - Spearman rank correlation ($\rho$) with fractional average ranking for tied observations;<br>   - Kendall rank correlation ($\tau$-b) with concordant ($P$) and discordant ($Q$) pair computation and analytical tie adjustments $T_x, T_y$;<br>   - Rigorous $p$-value derivation for two-tailed and one-tailed hypotheses via Student&#39;s $t$ survival function (Pearson and Spearman) and asymptotic normal $Z$ statistics (Kendall);<br>   - Automatic significance flag annotations in matrix cells (`*` at $p &lt; 0.05$, `**` at $p &lt; 0.01$);<br>   - Missing value handling: pairwise and listwise case exclusions;<br>   - **Never Crash** protection: safe handling of zero-variance constants, degenerate pairs, and small sample edge cases ($N &lt; 2$) on 100% safe Rust;<br>   - **Golden Oracle:** Test suite `correlations_tests.rs` verifying correlation matrices and significance values against Python `scipy.stats` (`pearsonr`, `spearmanr`, `kendalltau`) within $\le 10^{-6}$ precision.<br>2. **Command Bus &amp; Syntax L5 (`statcraft_syntax::commands::correlations_cmd`):**<br>   - Typed engine command `CorrelationsCommand` (`stat.correlations`) with JSON parameter specs for external AI agents;<br>   - Canonical IBM SPSS Statistics syntax emission (`CORRELATIONS /VARIABLES=... /PRINT=TWOTAIL SIG /STATISTICS DESCRIPTIVES XPROD /MISSING=PAIRWISE.` and `NONPAR CORR`).<br>3. **User Interface L6 (`statcraft_app::dialogs::correlations_dialog`):**<br>   - Modal dialog `CorrelationsDialog` ($560 \times 430$ px) built with `DialogKit`:<br>     * Source variables picker (`VariablePicker`) with scale measurement icons;<br>     * Vector transfer button (`TransferButton`);<br>     * Target variables list `Variables:`;<br>     * `Correlation Coefficients` checkboxes (Pearson, Kendall&#39;s tau-b, Spearman);<br>     * `Test of Significance` radio group (Two-tailed / One-tailed) and `Flag significant correlations` checkbox;<br>     * Right sidebar (`SubdialogSidebar`) with `[ Options... ]` button;<br>     * Modal subdialog `Options` (Statistics: Means and standard deviations, Cross-product deviations and covariances; Missing Values: Exclude cases pairwise / listwise) with `SubdialogActionBar`;<br>     * Standard bottom action bar `DialogActionBar` (`[ OK ] [ Paste ] [ Reset ] [ Cancel ] [ Help ]`).<br>4. **Summary Pivot Tables in Output Viewer (`tables_correlations.rs`):**<br>   - **Descriptive Statistics:** Variable, Mean, Std. Deviation, $N$;<br>   - **Correlations Matrix Table:** multi-level $K \times K$ grid presenting correlation coefficients with asterisks, exact significance, $N$, optional cross-product deviations, sample covariances, and footnote legends;<br>   - TSV clipboard export for spreadsheet workflows and Outline Pane integration.<br>5. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - Full automated CI gate passed (`cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci` — 100% OK);<br>   - 100 workspace unit and integration tests passing with 0 failures;<br>   - Architectural linters (`design-guard`, `file-guard`, `layers`, `parity`) reporting 0 violations;<br>   - Strict compiler linter `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -j 1 -- -D warnings` — 0 warnings;<br>   - Code formatting `cargo fmt --check` — completely clean.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 7.3: Two-Independent-Samples Nonparametric Tests (Mann-Whitney $U$ &amp; Wilcoxon $W$)</h3><p>*Time: October 29, 2026, 07:35 (~35 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented the fundamental distribution-free alternative to the independent-samples t-test for comparing two continuou