istics (Sign Test):** Exact Sig. (2-tailed);<br>   - TSV clipboard export and Outline Pane integration.<br>5. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - Full automated CI gate passed (`cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci` — 100% OK);<br>   - 110+ workspace unit and integration tests passing;<br>   - Architecture, design, and file-guard linters reporting 0 violations;<br>   - Compiler linter `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -j 1 -- -D warnings` — 0 warnings;<br>   - Code formatting `cargo fmt --check` — completely clean.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 7.5: Navigation Panel Overflow Fix &amp; Kruskal-Wallis $H$ Test for $K$ Independent Samples</h3><p>*Time: October 29, 2026, 08:45 (~35 minutes)*</p><p>Completed two major objectives: resolved the navigation title text overflow defect in the Output Viewer Outline Pane and implemented the nonparametric one-way ANOVA counterpart — **Kruskal-Wallis $H$ Test for Several Independent Samples** (`Analyze -&gt; Nonparametric Tests -&gt; K Independent Samples...`):<br>1. **Outline Navigation Overflow Defect Fix:**<br>   - Root Cause: low-level `ui.painter().text(...)` calls in `crates/statcraft_app/src/views/output_view/outline.rs` rendered text beyond boundaries without width clipping, and the parent container lacked clipping;<br>   - Solution:<br>     1. Increased navigation panel base width `outline_width` from 200.0 to 230.0 px for enhanced readability on high-DPI displays;<br>     2. Enforced rigid clipping boundary `ui.set_clip_rect(left_rect)` on the tree viewport;<br>     3. Implemented per-character ellipsis utility `truncate_text_to_width` using `ui.fonts` measurements to append `...` if text exceeds available width;<br>     4. Enclosed text painting in `ui.painter().with_clip_rect(text_rect)`;<br>     5. Added `.on_hover_text(...)` tooltips presenting complete untruncated titles on hover.<br>2. **Mathematical Engine L2 (`statcraft_algo::kruskal_wallis` &amp; `kruskal_wallis_tests`):**<br>   - Numeric range filtering for grouping variable $[min, max]$ following SPSS canon `BY groupvar(min max)`;<br>   - Combined ranking across all $N = \sum n_i$ cases with mid-ranks for ties;<br>   - Group rank sums $R_i$ and mean ranks $\bar{R}_i = R_i / n_i$ across all $k$ groups;<br>   - Raw Kruskal-Wallis statistic $H = \frac{12}{N(N+1)} \sum \frac{R_i^2}{n_i} - 3(N+1)$;<br>   - Tie correction factor $C = 1 - \frac{\sum (t_j^3 - t_j)}{N^3 - N}$ and adjusted statistic $H_{adj} = H / C$;<br>   - Degrees of freedom $df = k - 1$ and asymptotic 2-tailed $p$-value from $\chi^2$ distribution (`chi_square_sf(H_adj, df)`);<br>   - **Golden Oracle:** Test suite `kruskal_wallis_tests.rs` verified against Python `scipy.stats.kruskal` to $\le 10^{-6}$ precision for both unique and tied distributions;<br>   - **Never Crash** protection for empty datasets, single groups ($k &lt; 2$), and degenerate cases on 100% safe Rust.<br>3. **Command Bus &amp; Syntax L5 (`statcraft_syntax::commands::kruskal_wallis_cmd`):**<br>   - Typed engine command `KruskalWallisCommand` (`stat.npar.kruskal_wallis`) with JSON parameter specs for external AI agents;<br>   - Canonical SPSS syntax generator:</p><p><em>[code block — open in CapsuleCraft web for its canvas]</em></p><p>4. **User Interface L6 (`statcraft_app::dialogs::kruskal_wallis_dialog` &amp; `kruskal_define_range`):**<br>   - Modal dialog `Tests for Several Independent Samples` ($560 \times 430$ px) built with `DialogKit`:<br>     * Available variables list `VariablePicker` with scale icons;<br>     * `Test Variable List:` target list and `Grouping Variable:` display box showing range `var(min max)`;<br>     * Adaptive vector transfer buttons `TransferButton`;<br>     * Right sidebar `SubdialogSidebar` with `[ Define Range... ]` button;<br>     * Modal subdialog `Define Range` ($360 \times 300$ px) using `DialogShell::subdialog` with `Minimum:` and `Maximum:` fields;<br>     * `Test Type` group box with `[x] Kruskal-Wallis H` checkbox;<br>     * Bottom action bar 