es` / syntax `WEIGHT BY var.` / `WEIGHT OFF.`):</p><p>1. **Weighting Model in DataSet L1 (`statcraft_core::dataset`):**<br>   - Added `weight_var: Option&lt;String&gt;` to `DataSet` accompanied by `set_weight_variable()`, `weight_var()`, `is_weighted()`, and `row_weight(row_idx)`;<br>   - Enforced strict canonical SPSS rules: case weights must be non-negative ($w_i \ge 0$), while cases with zero ($w_i = 0$), negative ($w_i &lt; 0$), or missing values (`NaN` / `SYSMIS`) are systematically excluded from computations;<br>   - Seamless synergy with `Select Cases`: when row filtering is active, weights are applied exclusively to active observations (`active_row_indices`), preventing statistical bias;<br>   - Metadata synchronization: variable deletion (`remove_variable`) or renaming (`rename_variable`) safely updates or clears the weight state with zero panics.</p><p>2. **Mathematical Core L2 (`statcraft_algo`):**<br>   - **Frequencies (`frequencies.rs`):** weighted category frequencies ($f_w = \sum w_i$), weighted valid and cumulative percentages, and weighted percentile/quartile distribution analysis;<br>   - **Descriptive Statistics (`descriptives.rs`):** `compute_descriptives_weighted` routine computing weighted mean $\bar{x}_w = \frac{\sum w_i x_i}{\sum w_i}$, weighted sample variance $s_w^2 = \frac{\sum w_i (x_i - \bar{x}_w)^2}{W - 1}$ (where $W = \sum w_i$), standard error of the mean, weighted skewness, and weighted kurtosis;<br>   - **Crosstabs (`crosstabs.rs`):** weighted $R \times C$ contingency tables, marginal totals, and Pearson&#39;s Chi-Square test of independence incorporating frequency weights;<br>   - 100% safe Rust, zero runtime overhead when weighting is disabled.</p><p>3. **Command Bus &amp; Syntax L5 (`statcraft_syntax::commands::weight_cases_cmd`):**<br>   - Strongly-typed `WeightCasesCommand` (`data.weight_cases`) with parameter `specs()` for AI agents;<br>   - Canonical SPSS syntax generator:</p><p><em>[code block — open in CapsuleCraft web for 