ability Analysis (Cronbach&#39;s Alpha) for comprehensive psychometric and multivariate validation:</p><p>1. **Mathematical Engine L2 (`statcraft_algo::factor`, `factor_types`, `factor_tests`):**<br>   - Listwise missing case deletion and observation weighting (`row_weight`) support;<br>   - Computation of pairwise Pearson correlations and weighted correlation matrix $R$ ($p \times p$);<br>   - Factorability and sampling adequacy diagnostics:<br>     * **Kaiser-Meyer-Olkin (KMO) Measure of Sampling Adequacy**: anti-image partial correlation calculation $a_{ij} = -s_{ij} / \sqrt{s_{ii} s_{jj}}$ via numerical inversion of $S = R^{-1}$ and $\text{KMO} = \frac{\sum_{i \ne j} r_{ij}^2}{\sum_{i \ne j} r_{ij}^2 + \sum_{i \ne j} a_{ij}^2}$;<br>     * **Bartlett&#39;s Test of Sphericity**: $\chi^2 = -(n - 1 - (2p + 5)/6) \ln |R|$ at $df = p(p - 1)/2$ with exact $p$-value from Chi-square survival function;<br>   - Principal Component Analysis (**PCA**) Extraction:<br>     * Spectral decomposition of real symmetric matrix $R$ via cyclic Jacobi rotations on 100% safe Rust without external linear algebra dependencies (`jacobi_eigen_symmetric`);<br>     * Kaiser criterion ($\lambda \ge 1.0$) or fixed factor count extraction;<br>     * Deterministic sign convention for positive dominant loadings;<br>     * Factor loadings $l_{ik} = \sqrt{\lambda_k} \cdot v_{ik}$;<br>     * Communalities (*Communalities*): initial 1.000 for PCA, extraction $h_i^2 = \sum_{k=1}^m l_{ik}^2$;<br>     * Total Variance Explained (*Total Variance Explained*): initial eigenvalues, % of variance, cumulative %, and extraction sums of squared loadings;<br>     * Component Matrix (*Component Matrix*);<br>   - **Golden Oracle:** `factor_tests.rs` unit tests verified against Python `scipy.linalg.eigh` and `factor_analyzer` with precision $\le 10^{-6}$;<br>   - **Never Crash** protection against singular matrices, $n &lt; 2$, zero-variance variables, and missing cases.</p><p>2. **Command Bus &amp; Syntax L5 (`statcraft_syntax::commands::factor_cmd`):**<br>   - Typed engine command `FactorCommand` (`stat.factor`) with JSON parameter specs for external AI agents;<br>   - Canonical IBM SPSS Statistics syntax generator and parser:</p><p><em>[code block — open in CapsuleCraft web for its canvas]</em></p><p>- Full `Undo` / `Redo` lifecycle support.</p><p>3. **DialogKit Desktop User Interface L6 (`statcraft_app::dialogs::factor_dialog`):**<br>   - Centered canonical modal dialog ($560 \times 430$ px, `DialogShell::standard`);<br>   - Two-panel `VariablePicker` with measurement scale icons and vector transfer buttons `TransferButton` (`-&gt;` / `&lt;-`);<br>   - `Variables:` target list (requires at least 2 items to enable `[ OK ]`);<br>   - Right sidebar `SubdialogSidebar` with modal configuration triggers:<br>     * `[ Descriptives... ]`: subdialog with `[x] KMO and Bartlett&#39;s test of sphericity`;<br>     * `[ Extraction... ]`: subdialog with PCA method and factor retention criteria (Eigenvalues over 1.0 / Fixed number of factors);<br>     * Action row `SubdialogActionBar` (`[ Continue ] [ Cancel ] [ Help ]`);<br>   - Canonical bottom action bar `DialogActionBar` (`[ OK ] [ Paste ] [ Reset ] [ Cancel ] [ Help ]`).</p><p>4. **Summary Pivot Tables in Output Viewer (`tables_factor.rs`):**<br>   - **KMO and Bartlett&#39;s Test:** Kaiser-Meyer-Olkin Measure of Sampling Adequacy, Bartlett&#39;s Test of Sphericity (Approx. Chi-Square, df, Sig.);<br>   - **Communalities:** Variable, Initial (1.000), Extraction;<br>   - **Total Variance Explained:** Component, Initial Eigenvalues (Total, % of Variance, Cumulative %), Extraction Sums of Squared Loadings;<br>   - **Component Matrix:** variables $\times$ components;<br>   - TSV clipboard export and Outline Tree integration.</p><p>5. **Reactivity, Menu &amp; Status Bar:**<br>   - Activated main menu item `Analyze -&gt; Dimension Reduction -&gt; Factor...`;<br>   - Canonical syntax automatically recorded to Output Viewer (Log);<br>   - Sta