ardcoding (`locales/en.ftl`, `locales/ru.ftl`);<br>   - Compiler linter `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -j 1 -- -D warnings` — 0 warnings;<br>   - Release binary built and deployed to `C:\StatCraft\statcraft_app.exe`.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 12.1: Subgroup Means Breakdown and One-Way ANOVA (Subgroup Means Breakdown: `MEANS`)</h3><p>*Time: October 29, 2026, 19:40 (~45 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented the classical exploratory procedure for subgroup analysis of IBM SPSS Statistics — **Subgroup Means Breakdown** (`Analyze -&gt; Compare Means -&gt; Means...`), combining detailed cell-level summary statistics across factor levels, one-way analysis of variance (ANOVA), and measures of association:</p><p>1. **Mathematical Engine L2 (`statcraft_algo::means`, `means_types`, `means_tests`):**<br>   - Listwise missing case deletion per table and full support for observation weights (`row_weight`);<br>   - Natural sorting of group categories (numeric ordering for numeric groups, lexicographic for strings);<br>   - Complete set of cell statistics per group and for the overall Total row:<br>     * Case count ($N$), weighted mean ($\bar{x}$), unbiased standard deviation ($s$), sample variance ($s^2$);<br>     * Median (with proper linear interpolation), minimum ($\min$), maximum ($\max$), weighted sum of values ($\sum x$);<br>   - **One-Way ANOVA Table (ANOVA Table):**<br>     * Between Groups variation: $SS_{between} = \sum n_j (\bar{x}_j - \bar{x})^2$, $df = k - 1$;<br>     * Within Groups variation: $SS_{within} = \sum \sum (x_{ij} - \bar{x}_j)^2$, $df = N - k$;<br>     * Total variation: $SS_{total} = SS_{between} + SS_{within}$, $df = N - 1$;<br>     * Mean Squares ($MS$), Fisher&#39;s $F$-test ($F = MS_{between} / MS_{within}$), and exact $p$-value from Fisher distribution survival function (`f_distribution_sf`);<br>   - **Measures of Association:**<br>     * Coefficient of determination $\eta^2 = SS_{between} / SS_{total}$ (proportion of variance explained) and correlation ratio $\eta = \sqrt{\eta^2}$;<br>   - **Golden Oracle:** `means_tests.rs` unit tests verified against analytical standards and Python `scipy.stats.f_oneway` with precision $\le 10^{-6}$;<br>   - **Never Crash** resilience against empty samples, single-case groups ($N &lt; 2$), zero within-group variance, and missing data on 100% safe Rust.</p><p>2. **Command Bus &amp; Syntax L5 (`statcraft_syntax::commands::means_cmd`):**<br>   - Typed engine command `MeansCommand` (`stat.means`) with JSON parameter specs for external AI agents;<br>   - Canonical IBM SPSS Statistics syntax generator:</p><p><em>[code block — open in CapsuleCraft web for its canvas]</em></p><p>- Full `Undo` / `Redo` lifecycle support.</p><p>3. **DialogKit Desktop User Interface L6 (`statcraft_app::dialogs::means_dialog`):**<br>   - Centered canonical modal dialog ($560 \times 430$ px, `DialogShell::standard`);<br>   - Two-panel `VariablePicker` with measurement scale icons and adaptive vector transfer buttons `TransferButton` (`-&gt;` / `&lt;-`);<br>   - Target lists `Dependent List:` and `Layer 1 of 1:` (independent factor variables);<br>   - Right sidebar `SubdialogSidebar` with `[ Options... ]` button:<br>     * Modal subdialog for selecting statistics (Mean, Number of Cases, Std. Deviation, Variance, Median, Minimum, Maximum, Sum) and checkbox `[x] Anova table and eta`;<br>     * Action row `SubdialogActionBar` (`[ Continue ] [ Cancel ] [ Help ]`);<br>   - Canonical bottom action bar `DialogActionBar` (`[ OK ] [ Paste ] [ Reset ] [ Cancel ] [ Help ]`).</p><p>4. **Summary Pivot Tables in Output Viewer (`tables_means.rs`):**<br>   - **Case Processing Summary:** Dependent $\times$ Grouping, Included ($N$, %), Excluded ($N$, %), Total ($N$, %);<br>   - **Report:** factor level breakdown with statistics (Mean, N, Std. Deviation, Variance, Median, Minimum, Maximum, Sum) and summary Total row;<br>   - **ANOVA Table:** Sum of Squares, df, Mean Square, F, Sig. for Between Groups, Within Groups, and Total;<br>   - **Measures of Association:** Eta, Eta Squared;<br>   - TSV clipboard export and Outline Tree integration.</p><p>5. **Reactivity, Menu &amp; Status Bar:**<br>   - Activated main menu item `Analyze -&gt; Compare Means -&gt; Means...`;<br>   - Canonical syntax automatically recorded to Output Viewer (Log);<br>   - Status bar feedback notification (`Means breakdown computed for &lt;n&gt; case(s)`).</p><p>6. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - Full automated CI quality gate passed (`cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci` — 100% OK);<br>   - Strict adherence to file size limits (`file-guard` $\le 500$ lines on leaf modules);<br>   - Strict adherence to DialogKit standards (`design-guard` — 100% compliant);<br>   - Architectural and parity linters (`layers`, `parity` — 39 documented procedures) reporting 0 violations;<br>   - Synchronous trilingual localization without string hardcoding (`locales/en.ftl`, `locales/ru.ftl`, `C:\StatCraft\locales\fr.ftl`);<br>   - Compiler linter `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -j 1 -- -D warnings` — 0 warnings;<br>   - Release binary built and deployed to `C:\StatCraft\statcraft_app.exe`.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase MP-1: Session Lifecycle &amp; File Menu Navigation</h3><p>*Time: October 29, 2026, 21:30 (~25 minutes)*</p><p>Activated core session lifecycle and navigation items in the main `File` menu of StatCraft (`crates/statcraft_app`), transitioning them from `MenuItemStatus::InDev` to fully operational `MenuItemStatus::Ready`:<br>1. **Recent Files Manager L6 (`recent_files.rs`):**<br>   - `RecentFiles` queue data structure maintaining up to 10 recently opened files;<br>   - Automatic rotation: accessed files are prepended to the top, duplicates promoted, older entries beyond 10 truncated;<br>   - Dual persistence: saving to `.statcraft/recent_files.json` and integrating with `eframe::Storage` upon shutdown;<br>   - Interactive submenu `File -&gt; Recent Files`: path tooltips on hover, disabled placeholder `(No recent files)` when empty, and separator with `Clear Recent Files`.<br>2. **Session Lifecycle Coordination L6 (`app_session.rs`):**<br>   - `File -&gt; New -&gt; Data` (`Ctrl+N`): clears current dataset to a blank sheet, resets `current_file_path`, resets `CommandBus` history and active filter/weight/split states, activates `Data View` tab, reports to status bar, and appends `NEW DATASET.` to the `Output Viewer` Log;<br>   - `File -&gt; New -&gt; Syntax`: shifts focus to the `Syntax Editor` tab, initializes canonical header `* StatCraft Syntax Editor. / * Created: &lt;timestamp&gt;.`, reports status;<br>   - `File -&gt; New -&gt; Project` (`Ctrl+Shift+N`): full state reset (dataset, output viewer log, syntax editor, active path);<br>   - `File -&gt; Close Project`: resets active project state, restores status bar to `Ready`;<br>   - Unsaved changes guard `has_unsaved_changes()`: modal confirmation `ConfirmSaveDialog` (`[ Save ] [ Don&#39;t Save ] [ Cancel ]`) built on `DialogShell::subdialog` prevents accidental loss of data.<br>3. **Syntax Editor Interactive Screen L6 (`views/syntax_editor.rs`):**<br>   - Interactive view `SyntaxEditorState` and `render_syntax_editor`;<br>   - Monospace multiline code editor tab docked in the workspace (`Tab::SyntaxEditor`);<br>   - Shortcut navigation via `Window -&gt; Syntax Editor` (`Ctrl+4`).<br>4. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - Dedicated unit and integration test suite `crates/statcraft_app/tests/session_lifecycle_tests.rs` (queue rotation, change detection, session reset flows, headless rendering);<br>   - Full automated CI quality gate passed (`cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci` — 100% OK);<br>   - File guard compliance: coordinator `app.rs` stays strictly under limit (1407 of 1500 lines);<br>   - DialogKit design compliance `design-guard` — 100% OK;<br>   - Synchronous bilingual localization (`locales/en.ftl`, `locales/ru.ftl`);<br>   - Compiler linter `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -j 1 -- -D warnings` — 0 warnings.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase MP-3: Export Data &amp; Export Output Reports</h3><p>*Time: October 29, 2026, 22:15 (~35 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented complete export workflows for data and analysis outputs in the `File -&gt; Export` menu:<br>1. **Data Export L0/L1 (`statcraft_io::csv_writer`, `statcraft_core::csv_export`):**<br>   - L0 module `csv_writer.rs` supporting `CsvExportOptions` (comma, semicolon, tab delimiters, quote escaping, newline/carriage return handling, decimal comma conversion, and configurable missing value `sysmis_repr`);<br>   - L1 module `csv_export.rs` implementing `export_dataset_to_csv` for streaming `DataSet` export with value labels substitution (`ValueLabels`) or raw numeric codes, empty dataset safety (0 rows/cols), and streaming `std::io::Write`;<br>   - Save file dialog filters: `Comma-Separated Values (*.csv)`, `Tab-Delimited Values (*.tsv, *.txt)`, `Semicolon-Separated Values (*.csv)` with automatic delimiter resolution from path.<br>2. **Reporting Architectural Layer L4 (`crates/statcraft_reporting`):**<br>   - Created new standalone L4 layer crate `statcraft_reporting` (registered in `xtask/src/layers.rs` maintaining strict top-to-bottom hierarchy L4 $\to$ Utility, L6 $\to$ L4);<br>   - Universal reporting model: `ReportDocument`, `ReportSection`, `ReportItem` (Log, Notes, Table, Text, Warning), `ReportTable`, `ReportNotes`, `CellAlignment`;<br>   - HTML report generator `html_export.rs`: standalone single-file HTML5 document with authentic SPSS table styling (sans-serif typography, double header borders, zebra striping, accent procedure headings, italic footnotes, monospace syntax logs, and HTML entity escaping);<br>   - Monospace plain text generator `txt_export.rs`: ASCII border tables with dynamic column width calculation and text alignment;<br>   - TSV bundle generator `tsv_export.rs`: joins all session tables separated by double newlines for direct spreadsheet pasting (Excel, Google Sheets).<br>3. **User Interface &amp; Integration L6 (`crates/statcraft_app`):**<br>   - Module `views/output_view/export.rs`: converts `OutputViewerState` into `ReportDocument` across all statistical procedures;<br>   - Module `export_handlers.rs`: activates `File -&gt; Export -&gt; Export Output...` and `File -&gt; Export -&gt; Export Data...` (with `requires_dataset_status` availability guard);<br>   - Native OS save file dialogs via `rfd::FileDialog::save_file()`;<br>   - Status bar feedback notifications (`status-data-exported`, `status-output-exported`);<br>   - Syntax logging in `Output Viewer`: `SAVE TRANSLATE OUTFILE=&#39;...&#39; /TYPE=... /REPLACE /FIELDNAMES.` and `OUTPUT EXPORT /CONTENTS=ALL /TYPE=... /DESTINATION=&#39;...&#39;`.<br>4. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - 100% pass on full CI pipeline: `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci` (`fmt`, `clippy -D warnings`, `cargo test --workspace -j 1`, `parity`);<br>   - Strict layer validation `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- layers` (L4Reporting verification);<br>   - File size guard compliance `file-guard` ($\le 500$ lines on all new modules);<br>   - DialogKit design compliance `design-guard`;<br>   - Synchronous bilingual localization without string hardcoding (`locales/en.ftl`, `locales/ru.ftl`);<br>   - Test suites added for `statcraft_io::csv_writer`, `statcraft_core::csv_export`, `statcraft_reporting` (HTML, TXT, TSV), `statcraft_app::export_handlers`, and `output_view::export`.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase MP-5: SPSS Binary Data Files Import (.sav / .zsav)</h3><p>*Time: October 29, 2026, 22:20 (~30 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented full-featured import of original binary IBM SPSS Statistics files (`.sav` and compressed `.zsav`) with complete extraction of data matrices and dictionary metadata without relying on proprietary third-party libraries:<br>1. **Low-Level Binary Decoder L0 (`crates/statcraft_io::spss_loader`):**<br>   - Modular architecture: `header.rs`, `records.rs`, `decompress.rs`, `mod.rs` (each strictly $\le 500$ lines compliant with `file-guard`);<br>   - System Header Record 0 parsing (`$FL2` / `$FL3`, automatic endianness detection via `layout_code`, compression bias `bias = 100.0`, case weight index `weight_index`, case count `case_cnt`);<br>   - Variable Records Record 2 handling: numeric &amp; string variables, labels, user missing value specifications (discrete values, ranges);<br>   - Value Labels Records Record 3 &amp; 4: pairs `(f64, label)` mapped to target variable slots;<br>   - Extension Records Record 7: subtype 4 (Display parameters: Measure Scale/Ordinal/Nominal, alignment, column widths), subtype 13 (Long Variable Names mapping short 8-char names to UTF-8 names), subtype 20 (Character Encoding), subtype 24 (ZLIB chunk metadata for `.zsav`);<br>   - Bytecode streaming decompressor Record 999: opcode decoding 1..251 (`code - bias`), 252 (EOF), 253 (8-byte IEEE 754 floats or string literals), 254 (whitespace), 255 (system missing `SYSMIS` / `Null`);<br>   - Compressed `.zsav` support: reads `ztrailer`, streams block decompression via `flate2::read::ZlibDecoder` into uniform bytecode reader.<br>2. **Core Layer Integration L1 (`crates/statcraft_core::spss`):**<br>   - Module `spss.rs`: `DataSet::from_spss_data`, `DataSet::load_spss_from_path`, `DataSet::load_spss_from_reader`;<br>   - Converts `SpssVariableInfo` into `VariableMetadata`: 9 canonical SPSS types, `Measure`, `Alignment`, `ValueLabels`, `MissingValues`, and `weight_var`;<br>   - Typed error integration `CoreError::Io(#[from] statcraft_io::IoError)`.<br>3. **Command Bus L5 (`crates/statcraft_syntax`):**<br>   - Typed engine command `ImportSpssCommand` (`data.import_spss`) with JSON schema `specs()`, execution and Undo support;<br>   - Registered in `CommandBus::with_defaults()`;<br>   - SPSS syntax equivalent generator `GET FILE=&#39;&lt;path&gt;&#39;.`;<br>   - Transparent `.sav` and `.zsav` support added to `OpenFileCommand` (`data.open_file`).<br>4. **Desktop UI L6 (`crates/statcraft_app`):**<br>   - Activated menu item `File -&gt; Import Data -&gt; SPSS Data...` (`menu-file-import-spss`) with `SPSS Statistics Data (*.sav, *.zsav)` file dialog;<br>   - Added SPSS file filters to general `File -&gt; Open Data...` dialog (`open_data_dialog`);<br>   - `load_file_from_path` in `app_session.rs` automatically detects `.sav`/`.zsav`, loads dataset via command bus, logs `GET FILE=&#39;&lt;path&gt;&#39;.` into Output Viewer, updates `RecentFiles`, and focuses `Data View`.<br>5. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - 100% pass on CI quality gate: `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci` (`fmt`, `clippy -D warnings`, `cargo test --workspace -j 1`, `parity`, `layers`, `file-guard`, `design-guard`);<br>   - Unit tests in `statcraft_io::spss_loader::tests`: bytecode compression, uncompressed streams, corrupt header handling;<br>   - Session lifecycle integration test `crates/statcraft_app/tests/session_lifecycle_tests.rs::test_load_spss_sav_session_lifecycle`;<br>   - 100% bilingual localization (`locales/en.ftl`, `locales/ru.ftl`);<br>   - 100% Safe Rust without `unwrap`/`expect`/`panic` in non-test code.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase MP-2: Native Project Format (.stc) &amp; Save Commands</h3><p>*Time: October 29, 2026, 22:25 (~30 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented full native project format (`.stc`) persistence and file operations across the main `File` menu:<br>1. **Native Project Format Codec L0 (`statcraft_io::stc_codec`):**<br>   - Project container structure `StcContainer` (`format_version = 1`, `dataset_name`, `metadata_json`, `table: RawTable`, `active_filter_var`, `weight_var`, `split_file_json`);<br>   - Streaming Gzip compression via `flate2::write::GzEncoder` with automatic detection of the GZIP header (`0x1f 0x8b`) and fallback JSON deserialization on read;<br>   - Clean codec APIs: `save_stc_container`, `load_stc_container`, `save_stc_container_to_path`, `load_stc_container_from_path`;<br>   - CSV/TSV table export `crates/statcraft_io/src/csv_writer.rs` (`export_raw_table_to_csv_path`) with localized decimal separator and escaping support.<br>2. **Comprehensive Metadata Dictionary Serialization L1 (`statcraft_core::stc_codec`):**<br>   - 100% loss-free serialization and restoration of dataset state:<br>     * All 9 canonical SPSS variable data types (`Numeric`, `Comma`, `Dot`, `Scientific`, `Date`, `Dollar`, `CustomCurrency`, `String`, `RestrictedNumeric`);<br>     * Measurement scales (`Scale`, `Ordinal`, `Nominal`), text alignments (`Left`, `Right`, `Center`), column widths, and decimal digits;<br>     * Complete value label dictionaries `ValueLabels` (`BTreeMap&lt;String, String&gt;`);<br>     * Discrete and range missing values `MissingValues`;<br>     * Active filter configuration (`active_filter_var`), frequency weight variable (`weight_var`), and split-file settings (`split_file`);<br>   - Unified methods: `save_stc_to_writer`, `load_stc_from_reader`, `save_stc_to_path`, `load_stc_from_path`, and `save_csv_to_path`.<br>3. **Command Bus &amp; Canonical Syntax L5 (`statcraft_syntax::commands::file_cmds`):**<br>   - Save command `SaveFileCommand` (`data.save_file`) with parameter specs `specs()` and canonical syntax generator `SAVE OUTFILE=&#39;&lt;path&gt;&#39;.\nEXECUTE.`;<br>   - Open command `OpenFileCommand` (`data.open_file`) with syntax generator `GET FILE=&#39;&lt;path&gt;&#39;.\nEXECUTE.`;<br>   - Default registration in `CommandBus::with_defaults()`.<br>4. **Main Menu &amp; Native Dialog Integration L6 (`statcraft_app::app_session` &amp; `app.rs`):**<br>   - Transitioned menu items `File -&gt; Save` (`Ctrl+S`), `File -&gt; Save As...` (`Ctrl+Shift+S`), `File -&gt; Save Data As...`, `File -&gt; Open Project...` (`Ctrl+Shift+O`), `File -&gt; Open Data...` (`Ctrl+O`) to `MenuItemStatus::Ready`;<br>   - Native system file dialog integration via `rfd::FileDialog` with file extensions, filters, and smart default filenames;<br>   - Responsive keyboard shortcuts in `update()` (`Ctrl+S` -&gt; `save_project`, `Ctrl+Shift+S` -&gt; `save_project_as`, `Ctrl+Shift+O` -&gt; `open_project_dialog`);<br>   - Dynamic window title displaying the active file name and dirty state indicator `*`;<br>   - Automatic `RecentFiles` queue tracking and Output Viewer log recording (`SAVE OUTFILE=...` / `GET FILE=...`);<br>   - Safe session transition guard: prompt to save project before creating/opening new projects via `ConfirmSaveDialog`.<br>5. **Architectural Decomposition (&quot;Divide, don&#39;t prune&quot;):**<br>   - Extracted status message coordination into `crates/statcraft_app/src/status_message.rs`, slimming `app.rs` from 1453 down to ~1300 lines, ensuring healthy safety margin under the 1500 line limit.<br>6. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - Full automated CI quality gate passed (`cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci` — 100% OK);<br>   - 202 Rust files verified within strict size limits (`file-guard` — 100% OK);<br>   - Architecture layer rules `layers` (L0-L6) and design rules `design-guard` — 100% compliant;<br>   - 125+ workspace unit and integration tests passing;<br>   - 100% synchronous localization (`locales/en.ftl`, `locales/ru.ftl`);<br>   - Compiler linter `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -j 1 -- -D warnings` — 0 warnings.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase MP-4: Microsoft Excel Import (.xlsx / .xls / .ods)</h3><p>*Time: October 29, 2026, 23:05 (~35 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented direct tabular data reading and importing from Microsoft Excel and OpenDocument spreadsheets without needing prior conversion to CSV:<br>1. **I/O Layer L0 (`statcraft_io::excel_loader`):**<br>   - Integrated modern crate `calamine = &quot;0.37&quot;` (100% safe Rust, memory-efficient streaming parser without COM or Office dependencies);<br>   - Functions `load_excel_from_path`, `load_excel_from_reader`, and `load_excel_from_range` supporting `.xlsx`, `.xlsm`, `.xls`, `.ods`;<br>   - Worksheet parsing engine:<br>     * Default selection of the first sheet (`workbook.sheet_names()[0]`) or by explicit sheet name;<br>     * Canonical SPSS variable name sanitization and deduplication (`sanitize_and_dedup_headers`): invalid character conversion to `_`, `V_` prefix for leading digits, `VAR00001` generation for empty headers, and sequential `_1`, `_2` disambiguation;<br>     * High-fidelity cell type mapping from `calamine::Data` (integers `Int`, floats `Float`, booleans `Bool` -&gt; `1.0`/`0.0`, dates/times `DateTime`/`DateTimeIso`, strings `String`, empty/error cells `Empty`/`Error`/`&quot;NA&quot;`/`&quot;.&quot;` -&gt; `RawValue::Null`);<br>     * Automated column type inference: columns where all non-null values parse as numbers are typed as `RawDataType::Numeric`, while mixed columns cast numbers to formatted text as `RawDataType::Text`;<br>   - **Never Crash** guarantees: robust handling of empty workbooks, 0-row sheets, and header-only sheets without panics.<br>2. **Command Bus &amp; Syntax L5 (`statcraft_syntax::commands::import_excel`):**<br>   - Strongly-typed `ImportExcelCommand` (`data.import_excel`) with parameter specification `specs()` (`file_path`, `sheet_name`, `dataset_name`) for external AI agents;<br>   - Direct population of active `DataSet` with full `Undo` support (dataset reset);<br>   - Registered in default command bus `CommandBus::with_defaults()`.<br>3. **User Interface &amp; Integration L6 (`crates/statcraft_app`):**<br>   - Activated menu items `File -&gt; Import Data -&gt; Excel...` (`menu-file-import-excel`) and `File -&gt; Import Data -&gt; CSV...` (`menu-file-import-csv`);<br>   - Added `open_excel_dialog` using `rfd::FileDialog` with filter `Excel Spreadsheets (*.xlsx, *.xls, *.ods, *.xlsm)`;<br>   - Enhanced `load_file_from_path`: automated detection of spreadsheet extensions, execution of `data.import_excel`, addition to `RecentFiles` queue;<br>   - Canonical syntax logging in Output Viewer:</p><p><em>[code block — open in CapsuleCraft web for its canvas]</em></p><p>- Real-time status bar notification: `Dataset imported: &lt;name&gt; (&lt;