ring or irregular numeric categories into consecutive integer codes ($1, 2, 3, \dots, K$) with automatic assignment of original values to value labels — `Transform -&gt; Recode -&gt; Automatic Recode...` (`transform.auto_recode` command / `AUTORECODE` syntax):<br>1. **L2 Algorithmic Foundation (`crates/statcraft_algo/src/auto_recode.rs`):**<br>   - Core function `compute_auto_recode` and ordering enumeration `AutoRecodeOrder` (`LowestValue`, `HighestValue`);<br>   - Detection of unique non-missing values (`RawValue::Number` and `RawValue::Text`), safely skipping missing data (`Null`, `NaN`, empty strings);<br>   - Sorting unique categories: ascending (`LowestValue`) or descending (`HighestValue`);<br>   - Sequential assignment of integer codes ($1.0, 2.0, \dots, K$);<br>   - Automatic generation of `ValueLabels` dictionary (`&quot;1&quot;` $\to$ original value, `&quot;2&quot;` $\to$ original value...);<br>   - 100% Safe Rust without panics (`unwrap`, `expect`) with comprehensive unit tests for string, numeric, and missing datasets.<br>2. **L5 Command Bus &amp; Syntax Translation (`crates/statcraft_syntax/src/commands/auto_recode_cmd.rs`):**<br>   - Strongly-typed `AutoRecodeCommand` (ID `transform.auto_recode`) registered in `CommandBus`;<br>   - JSON parameter `specs()` (array of `pairs` with `source_var` and `target_var`, `order` option);<br>   - Creating new numeric variables (`Numeric`, `decimals: 0`, `Measure::Nominal`) with generated `ValueLabels` dictionary or overwriting existing variables;<br>   - Full `Undo` (`Ctrl+Z`) support via `AutoRecodeUndoItem` history (`Created` / `Overwritten`);<br>   - Canonical IBM SPSS Statistics syntax generator:</p><p><em>[code block — open in CapsuleCraft web for its canvas]</em></p><p>(with `/DESCENDING` subclause for `HighestValue` order).<br>3. **Zero-Hardcode Localization (`locales/en.ftl`, `locales/ru.ftl`):**<br>   - Declarative translation keys: `dialog-autorecode-title`, `dialog-autorecode-variables`, `dialog-autorec