alogKit;<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- parity` — 47 commands registered;<br>   - `cargo test --workspace -j 1` — 100% passing tests across all crates;<br>   - `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` — 0 warnings.</p><p>---</p><h3>Microplan #6: Rank Cases — `transform.rank_cases`</h3><p>*Time: October 30, 2026, 07:50 (~35 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented the canonical case ranking and normal scores procedure from IBM SPSS Statistics — **Rank Cases...** (`Transform -&gt; Rank Cases...`, command ID `transform.rank_cases`):<br>1. **Mathematical Engine L2 (`statcraft_algo::rank_cases` and `rank_cases_tests`):**<br>   - Implemented `compute_ranks` function with complete tie resolution support (`TiesHandling`):<br>     - `Mean`: average rank of tied cases (SPSS default);<br>     - `Low`: lowest rank in the tie cluster;<br>     - `High`: highest rank in the tie cluster;<br>     - `Seq`: sequential ranks without tie formation;<br>   - Direction selection `RankDirection` (`Ascending` assigning rank 1 to the smallest value, `Descending` assigning rank 1 to the largest value);<br>   - Comprehensive spectrum of rank transformation types `RankType`:<br>     - `SimpleRank`: standard integers / midranks;<br>     - `FractionalRank`: fractional ranks $r / N$;<br>     - `FractionalPercent` / `Percentiles`: percentile ranks $(r / N) \times 100$;<br>     - `Ntiles(k)`: quantiles calculated via $\lceil (r \cdot k) / N \rceil$ (default 4 for quartiles);<br>     - Normal scores: Blom $((r - 3/8) / (w + 1/4))$, Tukey $((r - 1/3) / (w + 1/3))$, Rankit $((r - 1/2) / w)$, Van der Waerden $(r / (w + 1))$;<br>   - Clean implementation of standard normal inverse CDF `inv_normal_cdf` (Peter J. Acklam rational approximation with error $&lt; 10^{-9}$);<br>   - 100% Safe Rust, `RawValue::Null` missing cases preserved at original indices.<br>2. **Command Bus L5 (`statcraft_syntax::commands::rank_cases_cmd`):**<br>   - Engine command `RankCasesCommand` (`transform.rank_cases`) with parameter `s