nuous variable discretization algorithm `compute_visual_binning` and `compute_visual_binning_with_labels` based on a list of `Cutpoint` specifications (upper bound `upper_bound` and inclusion boundary `inclusive`);<br>   - Automated value labels generation according to SPSS conventions (`&quot;&lt;= 25000&quot;`, `&quot;25000 - 50000&quot;`, `&quot;&gt; 50000&quot;`);<br>   - Cutpoint generators for three canonical discretization strategies:<br>     - `generate_equal_width_cutpoints`: equal-width intervals with width $W = (max - min) / N$;<br>     - `generate_equal_percentile_cutpoints`: equal-percentile quantile binning (equal number of observations per bin) using the SPSS HAVERAGE percentile method;<br>     - `generate_stddev_cutpoints`: standard deviation intervals at $\pm 1\sigma, \pm 2\sigma$ around sample mean $\mu$;<br>   - 100% Safe Rust without `unwrap` in runtime code, safe preservation of missing cases `RawValue::Null`, and unit tests covering all methods and generators.<br>2. **Command Bus L5 (`statcraft_syntax::commands::binning_cmd`):**<br>   - Engine command `VisualBinningCommand` (`transform.visual_binning`) with JSON Schema `specs()`;<br>   - Creation and overwriting of numeric target variables with `Measure::Ordinal`, `DataType::Numeric { decimals: 0 }`, and attached `ValueLabels` dictionary;<br>   - Canonical SPSS syntax generation:</p><p><em>[code block — open in CapsuleCraft web for its canvas]</em></p><p>- Comprehensive `Undo` support (`Ctrl+Z`).<br>3. **DialogKit Desktop User Interface L6 (`statcraft_app::dialogs::binning_dialog` and `binning_cutpoints_dialog`):**<br>   - Canonical DialogKit modal dialog `VisualBinningDialog` (`DialogShell::standard`);<br>   - Left-hand variable picker `render_variable_list_panel`;<br>   - Right-hand control area: target variable name and label, upper endpoint inclusion radio buttons (*Included (&lt;=) / Excluded (&lt;)*), `Make Cutpoints...` subdialog trigger, manual cutpoint addition, and interactive `Cutpoint Grid` table with editable labels;<br>   - Subdialog `binning_cutpoints_dialog` (`DialogShell::subdialog`, `SubdialogActionBar`) for method selection and number of cutpoints;<br>   - Canonical Type 1 action bar `DialogActionBar` (`[ OK ] [ Paste ] [ Reset ] [ Cancel ] [ Help ]`);<br>   - Activated main menu item `menu-transform-visual-binning` (status `InDev` removed), integration in `app_dialogs_data.rs`, status bar feedback, and syntax logging to `Output Viewer`.<br>4. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - 100% Safe Rust, 0 panics;<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- layers` — 0 violations;<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- file-guard` — all 232 files within size limits;<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- design-guard` — all dialogs strictly conform to DialogKit;<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- parity` — command registered;<br>   - `cargo test --workspace -j 1` — 100% passing tests across all crates;<br>   - `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` — 0 warnings.</p><p>---</p><h3>Microplan #7: Replace Missing Values (RMV) — `transform.replace_missing`</h3><p>*Time: October 30, 2026, 09:15 (~30 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented the canonical IBM SPSS Statistics missing data imputation procedure — **Replace Missing Values...** (`Transform -&gt; Replace Missing Values...`, command ID `transform.replace_missing`):<br>1. **Mathematical Engine L2 (`statcraft_algo::replace_missing`):**<br>   - Implemented `impute_missing_values` supporting all five canonical SPSS imputation methods (`ImputationMethod`):<br>     - `SeriesMean` (SMEAN): imputes missing values with the mean of all valid cases in the series;<br>     - `MeanOfNearby(span)` (MEAN): mean of valid nearby values within window $[i - \text{span} .. i + \text{span}]$;<br>     - `MedianOfNearby(span)` (MEDIAN): median of valid nearby values within window $[i - \text{span} .. i + \text{span}]$;<br>     - `LinearInterpolation` (LINEAR): linear interpolation between preceding valid $(i_0, y_0)$ and succeeding valid $(i_1, y_1)$ values, with endpoint nearest-neighbor carry for edge missing cases;<br>     - `LinearTrendAtPoint` (TREND): linear regression trend $y = a + b \cdot x$ using case observation index $x_i = i + 1$;<br>   - Robust Never Crash protection: safe handling of edge missing cases, series consisting entirely of missing values, empty or single-element series using 100% safe Rust.<br>2. **Command Bus L5 (`statcraft_syntax::commands::replace_missing_cmd`):**<br>   - Engine command `ReplaceMissingCommand` (`transform.replace_missing`) with JSON Schema `specs()` for AI agents;<br>   - Appending new numeric columns (`DataType::Numeric { decimals: 2 }`, `Measure::Scale`) or replacing existing columns;<br>   - Canonical SPSS syntax generation:</p><p><em>[code block — open in CapsuleCraft web for its canvas]</em></p><p>- Comprehensive batch `Undo` support (`Ctrl+Z`) restoring original columns, metadata, and values.<br>3. **DialogKit Desktop User Interface L6 (`statcraft_app::dialogs::replace_missing_dialog`):**<br>   - Modal window designed according to DialogKit standards (`DialogShell::standard`, $560 \times 430$ px);<br>   - Left-hand source variable selection panel, central `TransferButton`, right-hand list of replacement rules `target -&gt; METHOD(source)`;<br>   - Variable name editing field with `Change` button, `GroupBox` method selection radio buttons, and integer `span` input for nearby point methods;<br>   - Canonical Type 1 action bar `DialogActionBar` (`[ OK ] [ Paste ] [ Reset ] [ Cancel ] [ Help ]`);<br>   - Main menu item `Transform -&gt; Replace Missing Values...` activated (status `[dev]` removed);<br>   - Bilingual Fluent localization (`dialog-missing-*`, `output-missing-executed`, `status-missing-executed` in `ru.ftl` and `en.ftl`).<br>4. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - 100% Safe Rust, 0 panics, 0 `unwrap` in production code;<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- layers` — 0 violations;<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- file-guard` — all 232 files strictly within line limits;<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- design-guard` — all dialogs strictly conform to DialogKit;<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- parity` — command registered in parity registry;<br>   - `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` — 0 warnings;<br>   - `cargo test --workspace -j 1` — 100% passing tests across the entire workspace.</p><h3>Microplan #10: Date and Time Wizard — `transform.date_time_wizard`</h3><p>*Time: October 30, 2026, 10:00 (~30 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented the canonical IBM SPSS Statistics date and time manipulation facility — **Date and Time Wizard...** (`Transform -&gt; Date and Time Wizard...`, command ID `transform.date_time_wizard`):</p><p>1. **Mathematical Core L2 (`statcraft_algo::date_time`):**<br>   - Module `crates/statcraft_algo/src/date_time.rs` (393 lines, strictly within the $\le 500$ lines limit);<br>   - Safe date and timestamp parsing without panics: supports ISO 8601, RFC 3339, `YYYY-MM-DD`, `DD.MM.YYYY`, `MM/DD/YYYY`, `YYYY/MM/DD`, formats with timestamps `HH:MM:SS`, and numeric unix timestamps or epochs;<br>   - Operation enum `DateTimeOperation`:<br>     - `ExtractPart(DatePart)`: extracts year (`Year`), month (`Month`), day (`Day`), hour (`Hour`), minute (`Minute`), second (`Second`), day of week (`DayOfWeek`, 1 = Sunday per SPSS standard), and quarter (`Quarter`);<br>     - `Difference { unit: DateUnit }`: computes exact calendar intervals between two dates in years, months, weeks, days, hours, minutes, or seconds;<br>     - `AddDuration { amount, unit }`: adds or subtracts time durations with automated leap-year adjustment (e.g., Jan 31 + 1 month = Feb 29 in a leap year);<br>     - `ConstructDate`: normalizes string or numeric data into standard canonical date format;<br>   - Full support for missing values (`RawValue::Null`) and unparseable input with null preservation and zero crashes.</p><p>2. **Command Bus L5 (`statcraft_syntax::commands::date_time_cmd