t --workspace -j 1` — 100% passing test suite across all workspace crates and invariant tests.</p><p>---</p><h3>Microplan #11: Optimal Binning — `transform.optimal_binning`</h3><p>*Time: October 30, 2026, 10:35 (~35 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented the supervised discretization procedure of continuous attributes from IBM SPSS Statistics — **Optimal Binning...** (`Transform -&gt; Optimal Binning...`, command ID `transform.optimal_binning`):</p><p>1. **Algorithmic Core L2 (`statcraft_algo::optimal_binning`):**<br>   - New module `crates/statcraft_algo/src/optimal_binning.rs` (289 lines, strictly $\le 500$ lines);<br>   - MDLP Discretization Algorithm (Minimum Description Length Principle, Fayyad &amp; Irani 1993):<br>     * Sorting of $(x_i, y_i)$ pairs by continuous feature $x$;<br>     * Entropy and Information Gain optimization: $\Delta Ent = Ent(S) - \frac{|S_1|}{|S|}Ent(S_1) - \frac{|S_2|}{|S|}Ent(S_2)$;<br>     * Minimum Description Length stopping rule: candidate cutpoint is accepted only when Information Gain exceeds model complexity threshold $\frac{\log_2(N - 1) + \Delta}{N}$;<br>     * Global Priority Queue to iteratively split intervals with maximal global gain while strictly enforcing `max_bins` (default 5, min 2);<br>     * Robust Never Crash handling of constant features, single-class targets, and missing values (`Null`);<br>     * Automated interval boundary labeling (`&lt;= bound`, `prev - curr`, `&gt; bound`) and `ValueLabels` dictionary generation.</p><p>2. **Engine Command Bus L5 (`statcraft_syntax::commands::optimal_binning_cmd`):**<br>   - Typed engine command `OptimalBinningCommand` (`transform.optimal_binning`) with JSON Schema `specs()` for MCP and AI agents;<br>   - Creation of new numeric columns with `Measure::Ordinal` and 0 decimals, attaching generated category labels `ValueLabels`;<br>   - Canonical IBM SPSS Statistics syntax generator:</p><p><em>[code block — open in CapsuleCraft web for its canvas]</em></p><p>- Full batch `Undo` support (`Ctrl+Z`) removing generated columns in reverse index order.</p><p>3. **DialogKit Desktop User Interface L6 (`statcraft_app::dialogs::optimal_binning_dialog`):**<br>   - Modal dialog constructed with `DialogKit` (`DialogShell::standard`, $560 \times 430$ px);<br>   - Left-hand source variable picker `render_variable_list_panel`;<br>   - Vector adaptive `TransferButton` buttons for variables to bin and the categorical guide variable;<br>   - Right-hand panel: variables list, guide variable slot with clear button, settings `GroupBox` with `max_bins` counter (2..20) and target prefix input (`OB_`);<br>   - Canonical Type 1 action bar `DialogActionBar` (`[ OK ] [ Paste ] [ Reset ] [ Cancel ] [ Help ]`);<br>   - Main menu item `Transform -&gt; Optimal Binning...` activated (status `[dev]` removed);<br>   - Handled in `app_dialogs_transform.rs`, status message `StatusMessage::OptimalBinningExecuted`, and log recording in `Output Viewer`.</p><p>4. **Architectural Decomposition for File Size Guard:**<br>   - Decomposed `StatCraftApp` menu rendering into an isolated package `crates/statcraft_app/src/app_menus/` (`mod.rs`, `file_edit_view.rs`, `data_transform.rs`, `analyze_etc.rs`), reducing `app.rs` from 1557 to 585 lines (below the 1500 ceiling);<br>   - Decomposed `date_time_dialog` into `date_time_dialog/` (`mod.rs`, `view.rs`), satisfying the $\le 500$ lines limit.</p><p>5. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - 100% Safe Rust, 0 panics and 0 unwraps in application code;<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- layers` — 0 violations;<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- file-guard` — all 245 files strictly within line limits;<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- design-guard` — 100% DialogKit compliance;<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- parity` — 51 documented commands;<br>   - `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` — 0 warnings;<br>   - `cargo test --workspace -j 1` — 100% passing test suite across the entire workspace.</p><p>---</p><h3>Version 0.2.0: 