between `en.ftl` and `ru.ftl`, zero raw strings in UI source code, dynamic runtime language switching without restart (`hyp_42: supported`). 4/4 `i18n_lint_test` passing;<br>   * **M-31 (Vector-First UI):** all scale icons (Scale ruler, Ordinal bars, Nominal circles), arrows, folders, and tables rendered via `ui.painter()`. Absolute prohibition of Unicode emoji and rare symbols prevents tofu glyphs (`□`) across all platforms (`hyp_43: supported`);<br>   * **M-32 (Session Guard):** dirty flag tracking with window title `*` indicator, `ConfirmSaveDialog` guard preventing unsaved data loss on exit or file open, robust `RecentFiles` (MRU) tracking. 12/12 `session_lifecycle_tests` passing (`hyp_44: supported`);<br>   * **M-33 (Packaging &amp; CI):** version `0.2.1` synchronized byte-for-byte across all 4 manifests (`Cargo.toml`, `installer.iss`, `Info.plist`, `control`), registered file associations (`.sav`, `.zsav`, `.stc`, `.sps`), and multi-platform CI release workflow for Windows (ZIP + Inno Setup installer), Linux (.deb + tar.gz), and macOS (DMG + .app bundle) (`hyp_45: supported`).</p><p>5. **Documentation Finalization &amp; Quality Control (DoD):**<br>   * Created official bilingual UI audit specifications: [`docs/SPSS_UI_CANON_AUDIT.md`](SPSS_UI_CANON_AUDIT.md) (EN) and [`docs/SPSS_UI_CANON_AUDIT_RU.md`](SPSS_UI_CANON_AUDIT_RU.md) (RU);<br>   * Updated [`docs/CHECKLIST.md`](CHECKLIST.md) and Craft Anything ledger;<br>   * 100% pass across all tests and linters: `cargo test --workspace -j 1`, `xtask design-guard`, `xtask file-guard` (267 files), `xtask layers` (L0–L6), `xtask parity`.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 57: Real-World Corpora &amp; Data Codecs Audit (Microplans C-01 — C-05)</h3><p>*Time: November 6, 2026, 16:50 (~45 minutes)*</p><p>Conducted an in-depth Clean-Room audit and resilience stress-testing suite for the data input/output codecs subsystem (`crates/statcraft_io`) across real-world and synthetic data corpora (`.sav`/`.zsav`, `.xlsx`/`.xls`/`.ods`, `.csv`/`.tsv`, `.stc`). Resolved critical hidden SPSS specification defects, engineered a zero-dependency national encoding transcoder, hardened CSV and Excel loaders, and implemented an automated corpus runner `cargo xtask test-corpus` featuring an 11-probe malformed input fuzzing harness validating the Never Crash invariant:</p><p>1. **SPSS Compressed Bytecode Opcode 254 Resolution (`BUG-003`, `statcraft_io::spss_loader::decompress`):**<br>   * **Identified Defect:** In SPSS compressed data streams, opcode 254 was mistakenly decoded to `None` (`SYSMIS`). According to the open GNU PSPP specification, opcode 254 designates an 8-byte field of zeros — representing floating-point numeric `0.0` (or 8 spaces for string fields), whereas system-missing `SYSMIS` is represented exclusively by opcode 255;<br>   * **Resolution:** Opcode 254 decoding mapped directly to `DecodedSlot::Numeric(Some(0.0))`. Numeric zeros in compressed SPSS files are now accurately preserved.</p><p>2. **SPSS Record Type 7 Canonical Subtypes &amp; Very Long Strings (`BUG-004`, `statcraft_io::spss_loader::records`):**<br>   * **Subtype 11 (Variable Display Parameters):** Corrected record matching to read variable measurement scale, display width, and text alignment from canonical Subtype 11 rather than legacy Subtype 4 (machine floating-point info), while maintaining backward fallback;<br>   * **Subtype 14 (Very Long String Declarations):** Implemented parsing for extended string declarations (`VAR=LENGTH\t`) exceeding the 255-byte slot barrier. In the case reader, continuation slot stitching (`type_code == -1`) now ensures lengthy respondent text is not truncated;<br>   * **Subtypes 3 &amp; 20 (Codepage &amp; UTF-8):** Added robust extraction of dataset codepage from Subtype 3 and UTF-8 flags from Subtype 20.</p><p>3. **Zero-Dependency National Character Transcoder (`statcraft_io::spss_loader::encoding`):**<br>   * Engineered a safe Rust character transcoder with zero external crate dependencies for legacy non-UTF-8 SPSS archives:<br>     - **Windows-1251 (Cyrillic):** complete mapping for Russian, Ukrainian, and Belarusian;<br>     - **Windows-1252 (Western European):** standard Western Latin character map;<br>     - **KOI8-R:** Russian Unix/Internet encoding;<br>   * Automatic graceful fallback to UTF-8 when codepage is unspecified; raw byte caching (`label_raw`, `RawValueLabelList`) enables accurate deferred transcoding.</p><p>4. **Excel Loader Hardening (`statcraft_io::excel_loader`):**<br>   * Added token recognition for `&quot;-&quot;` and `&quot;none&quot;` alongside spreadsheet formula errors (`#VALUE!`, `#REF!`, `#DIV/0!`, `#N/A`, `#NAME?`, `#NUM!`, `#NULL!`);<br>   * Sanitized variable header extraction: blank cell headers map to `VAR00001`, invalid symbols are replaced with `_`, and leading digits are prefixed with `V_`.</p><p>5. **RFC 4180 Compliant CSV Loader (`statcraft_io::csv_loader`):**<br>   * Added automatic UTF-8 BOM (`\u{FEFF}`) stripping;<br>   * Supported robust auto-detection of column delimiters: comma `,`, semicolon `;`, tab `\t`, and pipe `|`;<br>   * Verified multiline cell values, escaped quote parsing (`&quot;&quot;`), and lossless round-trip invariant.</p><p>6. **Corpus Testing Runner &amp; Fuzzing Harness (`xtask/src/corpus.rs`):**<br>   * Implemented `cargo xtask test-corpus [--dir &lt;PATH&gt;]` scanner for local corpus directories (`fixtures/corpus/`, `test_data/`);<br>   * Generated realistic synthetic fixture corpus (`valid_survey.csv`, `valid_survey.stc`, `multiline_bom.csv`, `pipe_delimited.csv`, `semicolon_european.csv`, `synthetic_clean.sav`, `synthetic_compressed.sav`, `synthetic_cyrillic.sav`, `corrupt_truncated.sav`, `corrupt_bad_magic.sav`);<br>   * Built an 11-probe in-memory malformed input fuzzing harness running under `catch_unwind` — 0 panics across all corruption vectors (100% Never Crash compliant).</p><p>7. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   * Published comprehensive bilingual evidentiary audit reports: [`docs/CORPUS_AUDIT_REPORT.md`](CORPUS_AUDIT_REPORT.md) (EN) and [`docs/CORPUS_AUDIT_REPORT_RU.md`](CORPUS_AUDIT_REPORT_RU.md) (RU);<br>   * Registered `BUG-003` and `BUG-004` in [`docs/BUGS_AND_ISSUES.md`](BUGS_AND_ISSUES.md);<br>   * Updated Section 57 in [`docs/CHECKLIST.md`](CHECKLIST.md);<br>   * 100% pass across all tests and linters: `cargo test --workspace -j 1` (all crates), `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -j 1 -- -D warnings` (0 warnings), `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci` (file-guard, design-guard, layers, parity, test-corpus — 100% OK).</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 58: Batch Syntax Engine (.sps) &amp; Clean-Room Evidentiary Audit (Microplans S-01 — S-05)</h3><p>*Time: November 6, 2026, 18:55 (~45 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented and audited according to the *IBM SPSS Statistics 24 Command Syntax Reference* a comprehensive batch command syntax parser and dispatcher (**Batch Syntax Engine &amp; Dispatcher**) in `crates/statcraft_syntax`. The engine delivers raw script `.sps` batch execution capabilities via `CommandBus`, activates the desktop `Syntax Editor` toolbar with real-time log echoing and statistical table insertion in `Output Viewer`, and guarantees a 100% reversible round-trip cycle `GUI -&gt; to_sps -&gt; SyntaxParser -&gt; CommandBus`:</p><p>1. **Command Block Lexer &amp; Tokenizer (`statcraft_syntax::syntax_parser::lexer`):**<br>   * Engineered streaming `SyntaxLexer` splitting script text into `RawCommandBlock` items bounded by command-terminating periods `.`;<br>   * Complete isolation of non-terminator periods: decimal fractions in floating-point numbers (`3.14`, `0.95`) and dots inside single (`&#39;path.sav&#39;`) and double (`&quot;model.v1&quot;`) quoted strings do not truncate commands;<br>   * Full support for quote escaping via doubling (`&#39;&#39;` and `&quot;&quot;`), with line and column tracking on unclosed string literals;<br>   * Recognition of comments beginning with `*` or the keyword `COMMENT` spanning until the terminating period.</p><p>2. **Subcommand &amp; Variable Range Parser (`statcraft_syntax::syntax_parser::parser`):**<br>   * Detection of compound command names (`SORT CASES`, `SPLIT FILE`);<br>   * Structured parsing of subcommands with leading slash `/` and positional clauses;<br>   * Parenthesized parameter tokenization (`GROUPS=gender(1 2)`, `CI(0.95)`, `salary (D)`);<br>   * Automatic expansion of variable ranges `VAR1 TO VAR5` matching sequential column order in active dataset `VariableDictionary`;<br>   * Expansion of the keyword `ALL` into all active dataset variables.</p><p>3. **Modular Command Dispatcher &amp; `CommandBus` Integration (`statcraft_syntax::syntax_parser::dispatcher`):**<br>   * Modular command mappers `mappers/stats.rs` and `mappers/data.rs` strictly below 500 lines;<br>   * Translation of parsed commands into strongly-typed `CommandBus::execute` calls with JSON parameters for 15+ procedures:<br>     - `DESCRIPTIVES`, `FREQUENCIES`, `CROSSTABS`, `T-TEST` (Independent, Paired, One-Sample);<br>     - `ONEWAY`, `CORRELATIONS`, `REGRESSION`, `RELIABILITY`, `FACTOR`, `MEANS`;<br>     - `SORT CASES`, `WEIGHT`, `FILTER`, `SPLIT FILE`, `COMPUTE`, `GET`, `SAVE`, `EXECUTE`.</p><p>4. **Batch Runner &amp; Desktop GUI Integration (`statcraft_app::syntax_runner`):**<br>   * Added interactive action toolbar in `Syntax Editor`: `[ Run All ]`, `[ Run Selection ]`, `[ Clear ]`;<br>   * When selection is empty, `[ Run Selection ]` executes the statement currently under the cursor;<br>   * Output Viewer echoing: each executed command block is logged into the report tree prefixed with `&gt; `;<br>   * Automated unpacking of statistical calculation results into interactive pivot tables in Output Viewer;<br>   * 100% zero-hardcode bilingual localization via Fluent semantic keys (`locales/en.ftl` and `locales/ru.ftl`).</p><p>5. **Evidentiary Clean-Room Audit, Fixtures &amp; Fuzzing (DoD):**<br>   * Created canonical test fixtures in `fixtures/syntax/` (`batch_analysis.sps`,