`, `CROSSTABS`, `T-TEST`, `ONEWAY`, `REGRESSION`, `RELIABILITY`);<br>     2. `statcraft_load_dataset`: direct injection of raw tabular data (CSV/TSV text) into active memory without intermediate disk files;<br>     3. `statcraft_list_variables`: inspection of variable dictionary metadata (measures, types, labels, missing values);<br>     4. `statcraft_get_data_preview`: preview sample of the first $N$ rows for rapid distribution checks;<br>     5. `statcraft_insert_output_note`: insertion of formatted analytical findings and scientific conclusion cards into the Output Viewer tree;<br>     6. `statcraft_set_active_tab`: intentional tab switching (`data`, `variable`, `output`, `syntax`) without stealing user focus.<br>   - JSON-RPC 2.0 wire protocol over local TCP socket `127.0.0.1:18493` (Loopback);<br>   - Non-blocking socket listener with clean `AtomicBool` exit and guaranteed socket liberation upon `Drop`.</p><p>2. **Long-Running Service in App (`statcraft_app::bridge_service`):**<br>   - Dedicated `BridgeService` managing the server lifecycle within `StatCraftApp`;<br>   - Inter-thread channels (`BridgeAppRequest` and `oneshot` responders) bridging the TCP server thread to the UI frame loop in `update()`;<br>   - Direct execution via `syntax_runner::run_syntax_batch` and `DataSet::from_raw_table`;<br>   - In-memory ring buffer `BridgeLogRing` holding up to 100 entries with zero disk footprint.</p><p>3. **Interactive Semantic Activity Log &amp; Dialog (`dialogs/mcp_bridge_dialog`):**<br>   - Modular dialog built on canonical `DialogKit` (`DialogShell::standard`, `GroupBox`, `SubdialogActionBar`);<br>   - 100% vector-first UI: circular status indicator (`ui.painter().circle_filled`) with dynamic colors (emerald green / amber / gray) and zero Unicode tofu emojis;<br>   - One-click copy buttons for MCP configuration and agent Skill prompts;<br>   - Semantic live activity log: stores typed `BridgeLogEvent` variants, enabling on-the-fly bilingual translation of historical log entries via Fluent catalogs (`en.ftl` / `ru.ftl`).</p><p>4. **CLI Flag and Agent Assistant Skill:**<br>   - Added `--mcp` CLI flag to `main.rs`: `statcraft.exe --mcp` launches a lightweight stdio MCP proxy without initializing DirectX/GUI;<br>   - Authored system skill `.agents/skills/statcraft-assistant/SKILL.md` documenting agent workflows, syntax rules, and data auditing scenarios.</p><p>5. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - 100% test pass across the entire workspace via `cargo test --workspace -j 1`;<br>   - Static architecture and design checks: `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- layers`, `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- file-guard` (289 files strictly within size limits), `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- design-guard`, and `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- parity`;<br>   - Strict compiler and linting gate: `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` (0 warnings).</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 62: StatCraft Bridge v2 — Autonomous Code Mode, Output Return &amp; Dynamic Self-Documentation</h3><p>*Time: November 7, 2026, 12:00 (~50 minutes)*</p><p>Delivered a comprehensive architectural modernization of the StatCraft Socket Bridge (Bridge v2), transforming the bridge interface into an **autonomous Code Mode (SPSS Syntax REPL)**. External AI agents (Claude, Antigravity, local LLMs) are now 100% self-sufficient without access to Rust source code or manual documentation:</p><p>1. **Closing the Feedback Loop (Code Mode REPL Output Return):**<br>   - Extended the batch syntax execution engine `syntax_runner::run_syntax_batch` with `SyntaxBatchOutcome { count: usize, output_text: String }`;<br>   - Formatted all newly created procedures (SPSS Pivot Tables: ANOVA, Descriptives, Frequencies, T-Tests, Regression, Reliability) into clean monospace ASCII tables via `export_procedures_to_txt` and returned them directly in the text body of `statcraft_run_syntax`;<br>   - External agents immediately receive exact sample sizes, means, standard errors, Student&#39;s $t$ and Fisher&#39;s $F$ statistics, exact $p$-values, and confidence intervals in their conversation context.</p><p>2. **Dynamic Self-Documentation &amp; MCP Resources (Zero-Manual-Docs):**<br>   - Implemented syntax commands `HELP.` (general catalog of analytical procedure categories) and `HELP &lt;COMMAND&gt;.` (canonical syntax template, subcommands, and usage examples, e.g. `HELP ONEWAY.`);<br>   - Registered `HelpCommand` (`util.help`) in `CommandBus`, making syntax help accessible through both the parser and direct command execution;<br>   - Added native MCP Resources support to the stdio bridge server (`statcraft.exe --mcp`):<br>     - `resources/list`: exposes dynamic resource descriptor `statcraft://syntax-reference`;<br>     - `resources/read`: dynamically compiles comprehensive syntax and procedure manuals via `statcraft_syntax::generate_full_syntax_reference()` directly from the binary;<br>   - Intelligent Self-Correction: when encountering an unknown command or typo, the parser evaluates Levenshtein distance against known commands and suggests the closest valid procedure (`Did you mean &#39;ONEWAY&#39;? Type &#39;HELP.&#39; for available commands.`).</p><p>3. **SPSS Variable Dictionary Syntax Mappers (`variables.rs`):**<br>   - Implemented syntax mappers for dataset variable metadata management:<br>     - `VARIABLE LEVEL varlist (SCALE | ORDINAL | NOMINAL).` -&gt; `&quot;var.set_measure&quot;`;<br>     - `VARIABLE LABELS var &#39;Label&#39;.` -&gt; `&quot;var.set_label&quot;`;<br>     - `VALUE LABELS var code &#39;Label&#39;.` -&gt; `&quot;var.set_value_labels&quot;`;<br>     - `MISSING VALUES var (val1, val2) | (low THRU high).` -&gt; `&quot;var.set_missing_values&quot;`;<br>   - Upgraded core commands `SetMeasureCommand`, `SetLabelCommand`, `VarSetValueLabelsCommand`, and `VarSetMissingValuesCommand` to accept variable names (`var_name`, `variables`, `assignments`) alongside column indices.</p><p>4. **Statistical Procedure Mapping Fixes:**<br>   - `ONEWAY`: aligned parameter keys with canonical `OneWayAnovaCommand` schema (`dependent_vars`, top-level `descriptives`, `homogeneity`, `ci`);<br>   - `RELIABILITY`: aligned variable list key with `variables`;<br>   - `FACTOR`: aligned variable list key with `variables`;<br>   - `MEANS`: lifted summary options (`cell_mean`, `cell_count`, `cell_stddev`, `anova`) to top-level command arguments.</p><p>5. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - 100% test pass across the workspace via `cargo test --workspace -j 1` (0 failures, 0 regressions);<br>   - New integration test suites: `syntax_bridge_v2_tests.rs` and `syntax_runner_and_output_tests.rs`;<br>   - Static linters and architectural guards: `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- layers`, `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- file-guard` (294 files strictly within limits), `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- design-guard`, `cargo fmt --check`;<br>   - Zero-warning compiler policy: `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` (0 warnings);<br>   - Refactored agent skill `.agents/skills/statcraft-assistant/SKILL.md` to guide agents toward autonomous Code Mode REPL workflows.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 63: Self-Sufficient Introspective Bridge Engine &amp; Universal Code Mode (Zero-Maintenance Introspective Bridge)</h3><p>*Time: November 7, 2026, 15:05 (~35 minutes)*</p><p>Eliminated the architectural bottleneck of manual command registry maintenance and hardcoded procedure matchers in the socket bridge and output runner. Established the core principle of **&quot;Write Once — Works for All Future Functions&quot;**:<br>1. **Live Runtime Introspection from Compiled Binary (Zero-Code Base Discovery):**<br>   - Extended `CommandBus::list_specs()` with categories and syntax keywords, generating a dynamic live catalog of all engine commands registered in the core;<br>   - Added `statcraft_list_commands` tool and `statcraft://commands` dynamic resource to `statcraft_bridge`: external agents receive the exact catalog of all available procedures and JSON parameter schemas on the fly, eliminating the need to read or guess the codebase;<br>   - Added `CommandBus::find_by_syntax_keyword` for dynamic command resolution.<br>2. **Universal Code Mode (`statcraft_execute_command` &amp; `RUN COMMAND` Directive):**<br>   - Added universal execution tool `statcraft_execute_command` to the MCP bridge and IPC protocol: agents can invoke any engine command by `command_id` and JSON arguments with automatic parameter validation;<br>   - Added universal syntax directive in `SyntaxParser` and `SyntaxDispatcher`:<br>     `RUN COMMAND &quot;&lt;command_id&gt;&quot; { &lt;json_params&gt; }.` (with `CALL &quot;&lt;command_id&gt;&quot; { ... }.` alias);<br>   - Every newly registered `EngineCommand` becomes instantly executable both directly through MCP and inside batch `.sps` syntax scripts without requiring dedicated syntax mappers.<br>3. **Universal Output Viewer Renderer (Zero-Match Fallback):**<br>   - Replaced hardcoded `match parsed.name.as_str()` in `syntax_runner.rs` with an open two-tier rendering model;<br>   - Introduced `OutputItemKind::GenericReport` and isolated rendering module `tables_generic.rs`: arbitrary command results are automatically formatted into SPSS-styled summary tables and key-value cards, recorded into the `OutputViewer` tree, and streamed to `output_text` in bridge responses;<br>   - Synchronously updated Fluent localization catalogs `locales/en.ftl` and `locales/ru.ftl` with `output-generic-title` and `output-table`.<br>4. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - 100% test pass across the workspace via `cargo test --workspace -j 1` (0 failures, 0 regressions);<br>   - Full pass of dialog and output viewer invariant suites: `cargo test -p statcraft_app --test dialog_invariants -j 1` and `output_viewer_invariants -j 1`;<br>   - Architecture and code guard verifications: `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- layers`, `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- file-guard` (295 files strictly within size limits), `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- design-guard`, and `cargo fmt --check`;<br>   - Strict compiler and linting gate: `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` (0 warnings);<br>   - Localization linter pass: `cargo test -p statcraft_i18n -j 1` (4/4 passed).</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 64: System Language Auto-Detection &amp; Session Storage Persistence (Auto-Locale &amp; Storage Persistence)</h3><p>*Time: November 7, 2026, 15:50 (~40 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented seamless adaptation of the application to the user&#39;s OS language environment and guaranteed reliable persistence of user settings across restarts:<br>1. **System Language Auto-Detection (`statcraft_i18n::detect`):**<br>   - Added an isolated autodetection module `detect.rs` in `statcraft_i18n` adhering strictly to the `file-guard` limit ($\le 500$ lines);<br>   - Tiered cascade for OS language discovery:<br>     1. `STATCRAFT_LANG` environment variable (explicit process override for CI/headless runs);<br>     2. Native OS API call via cached `sys-locale` (`GetUserDefaultLocaleName` on Windows, `CFBundleCopyLocalizationsForPreferences` on macOS, POSIX API on Linux);<br>     3. Standard POSIX environment variables `LC_ALL`, `LC_MESSAGES`, `LANG`;<br>   - Added language tag normalizer `normalize_language_tag` stripping encodings (`.UTF-8`), modifiers (`@euro`), and country subtags (`-RU`, `_US` $\to$ `ru`, `en`, `de`);<br>   - Automatic activation of detected language during initial catalog setup `I18nCatalog::new_with_defaults()` with graceful international fallback to English (`en`) for non-Russian locales.<br>2. **Ensure Initialized Guard:**<br>   - Functions `set_language`, `current_language`, `available_languages`, `language_name`, `reload_locales`, `tr`, and `tr_args` now guarantee catalog initialization via atomic flag `INITIALIZED`, preventing multi-thread race conditions.<br>3. **Session State Persistence in `eframe::Storage`:**<br>   - Introduced persistent storage keys in `crates/statcraft_app/src/app.rs`:<br>     * `STORAGE_KEY_LANGUAGE = &quot;statcraft_language&quot;`;<br>     * `STORAGE_KEY_BRIDGE_AUTOSTART = &quot;statcraft_mcp_bridge_autostart&quot;`;<br>   - In `StatCraftApp::save`, serialized the current language and bridge autostart flag on window close and autosave ticks;<br>   - In `StatCraftApp::new`, restored the user&#39;s explicitly selected language (taking precedence over system autodetection) and bridge autostart flag (defaulting to `true` for seamless pairing with AI agents);<br>   - Created dedicated integration test `crates/statcraft_app/tests/storage_persistence_test.rs` using `MockStorage` validating persistence of language and bridge autostart across sessions.<br>4. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - 100% test pass across workspace: `cargo test --workspace -j 1` (140+ unit and integration tests passing);<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- layers`, `file-guard` (296 files), `design-guard` — 0 violations;<br>   - `cargo fmt --check` and `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` — 0 warnings;<br>   - Optimized release binaries `target/release/statcraft_app.exe` and `target/release/statcraft.exe` compiled and synchronized.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 65: Universal Theme System (Dark, Light, System)</h3><p>*Time: November 7, 2026, 16:40 (~45 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented complete theme system support across the application — **Dark (Dark Pro)**, **Light (SPSS Classic Light)**, and **System (System Auto)** with persistent storage and autonomous out-of-the-box styling for all future windows:<br>1. **High-Performance Lock-Free Theme Engine (`statcraft_app::theme`):**<br>   * Added `ThemeMode` enum (`Dark`, `Light`, `System`) with automated `serde` serialization/deserialization;<br>   * Developed academic `LIGHT_PALETTE` (SPSS Classic Light): pure white background `#FFFFFF`, soft gray panels/dialogs background `#F7F8FA`, high-contrast header gray `#E9ECEF`, subtle cyan selection `#DDF4FF`, and accent blue `#0969DA`;<br>   * Guaranteed WCAG AAA contrast ratio: primary text to background $\ge 15.6:1$ (exceeding AAA $7:1$), muted text $\ge 5.1:1$ (exceeding AA $4.5:1$);<br>   * Built on 100% Safe Rust without mutexes or `unsafe`: global atomic flag `IS_DARK_MODE: AtomicBool` with `Ordering::Relaxed` delivers zero-allocation, instant static reference access to `&amp;DARK_PALETTE` / `&amp;LIGHT_PALETTE` on the hot egui frame rendering path.<br>2. **Exhaustive Codebase Migration (Zero-Core Hardcoding for Themes):**<br>   * Migrated all static `Tokens::BG_*`, `Tokens::TEXT_*`, `Tokens::BORDER` constants to dynamic accessor methods `Tokens::bg_app()`, `Tokens::bg_panel()`, `Tokens::border()`, `Tokens::text_primary()`, etc.;<br>   * Updated all 53 application source files across the workspace (DataView, VariableView, Output Viewer, Custom Titlebar, Toolbar, DialogKit, and all 16 statistical procedure dialogs);<br>   * **Autonomy Principle:** Any future window or dialog built using `DialogKit` or `Tokens::*()` automatically adopts the active theme without modifying the theme engine.<br>3. **FPS Guard &amp; Preference Persistence:**<br>   * In `StatCraftApp::update`, `ctx.set_visuals` and `theme::set_dark_mode` calls are protected by `applied_dark_mode != Some(is_dark)` caching, eliminating redundant egui style invalidations and protecting FPS;<br>   * Theme configuration persists in `eframe::Storage` under `STORAGE_KEY_THEME = &quot;statcraft_theme&quot;` and seamlessly restores on relaunch;<br>   * Menu `View -&gt; Theme` activated from `MenuItemStatus::InDev` stubs to active `ui.selectable_label` toggles with 100% Fluent key coverage `t!(&quot;menu-view-theme-*&quot;)`.<br>4. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   * Unit tests `theme::tests::test_theme_mode_switching` and `theme::tests::test_wcag_contrast` verify runtime switching and mathematical WCAG compliance;<br>   * Integration test `test_theme_mode_persistence_serialization` validates `ThemeMode` serde roundtrips;<br>   * 100% workspace test suite pass: `cargo test --workspace -j 1` (0 failures, 0 regressions);<br>   * Architecture and static guards: `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- layers`, `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- file-guard` (297 files within limits), `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- design-guard`, `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings`.</p><p>---</p><h3>Release v0.3.0: Network Bridge via MCP, Universal Themes &amp; Auto-Locale (Release v0.3.0)</h3><p>*Time: November 7, 2026, 16:55 (~30 minutes)*</p><p>Prepared and published the major release **StatCraft v0.3.0**, marking the application&#39;s transition into the era of direct AI agent-assisted statistics via the Model Context Protocol and unveiling the universal theme system:<br>1. **StatCraft Network Bridge &amp; Autonomous AI Copilot (Code Mode &amp; MCP):**<br>   * Implemented full-featured local TCP socket server (port 18493) and headless stdio MCP server (`statcraft.exe --mcp`);<br>   * Shipped comprehensive MCP toolset (`statcraft_run_syntax`, `statcraft_execute_command`, `statcraft_list_commands`, `statcraft_list_variables`, `statcraft_load_dataset`, `statcraft_get_data_preview`, `statcraft_insert_output_note`);<br>   * Users with zero SPSS experience can conduct rigorous statistical analyses in natural language using their favorite AI assistants (Antigravity, Claude, ChatGPT, Ollama), obtaining mathematically exact results ($\le 10^{-6}$ vs SciPy) while watching interactive tables update live on-screen;<br>   * Added an exhaustive explanatory spoiler to `README.md` and `README.ru.md` detailing the benefits and workflow of the bridge for general researchers.<br>2. **Universal Theme System (Dark, Light, System):**<br>   * Engineered academic `LIGHT_PALETTE` (SPSS Classic Light) with WCAG AAA contrast $\ge 15.6:1$;<br>   * Lock-free atomic switch `IS_DARK_MODE` (100% Safe Rust, zero overhead);<br>   * FPS Guard style caching and persistent preference storage in `eframe::Storage`.<br>3. **Version Synchronization v0.3.0 (Packaging